   "description": "<p><strong>Do you want to take on a new challenge?</strong></p> <p>We're supporting an innovative technology organisation developing advanced scientific and engineering products used around the world. As software continues to play an increasingly important role in product development, we're looking for a Software Engineer to join a collaborative R&D team working on complex desktop applications that interact closely with sophisticated hardware systems.</p> <p>This is an opportunity to work on challenging engineering problems, contribute to long-term product development and help shape the future direction of world-class technology.</p> <p><strong>THE OPPORTUNITY</strong></p> <p>You'll be responsible for developing and enhancing Windows-based desktop software used within advanced scientific and engineering systems. Working as part of a multidisciplinary team, you'll contribute to software design, architecture, implementation and testing whilst collaborating closely with other engineers across hardware, systems and software disciplines.</p> <p>This role would suit a Software Engineer who enjoys understanding how systems work beneath the surface and has experience building robust, maintainable software products rather than purely web-based applications.</p> <p><strong>WHAT YOU'LL BE DOING</strong></p> <ul> <li>Designing, developing and maintaining desktop software applications using C# and Microsoft technologies</li><li>Contributing to software architecture, application design and long-term technical direction</li><li>Developing robust and maintainable code using object-oriented design principles and recognised design patterns</li><li>Building software that interacts closely with complex hardware and engineering systems</li><li>Working within Agile development teams to deliver new product functionality and enhancements</li></ul> <p><strong>WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR</strong></p> <ul> <li>Strong commercial experience developing desktop applications using C#</li><li>Good understanding of object-oriented design, software architecture and design patterns</li><li>Experience developing multithreaded, concurrent or asynchronous applications</li><li>Experience designing software interfaces, APIs and maintainable application structures</li><li>Experience working on software products within engineering, scientific, instrumentation, medical device or hardware-focused environments</li></ul> <p><strong>DESIRABLE EXPERIENCE</strong></p> <ul> <li>WPF, XAML or MVVM</li><li>Windows desktop application development</li><li>Hardware integration, instrument control or data acquisition systems</li><li>Scientific, imaging, measurement or engineering products</li><li>Real-time or performance-critical software applications</li></ul> <p><strong>WE WANT YOU!</strong></p> <p>We're looking for engineers who enjoy solving complex problems and taking ownership of software design, rather than simply implementing requirements. If you have a passion for software engineering, enjoy working close to hardware and want to contribute to products that combine software, engineering and innovation, we'd love to hear from you.</p> <p>If you want to make a difference in return for excellent employee benefits and career development opportunities, then get in touch!</p> <p>If you receive suspicious outreach claiming to be from us, please contact us via the ManpowerGroup website.</p>",
