   "description": "<p>Senior Software Engineer (.NET)</p><p>£85,000 to £95,000 + bonus + comprehensive benefits</p><p><br></p><p>Our client, a high-growth fintech organisation delivering cutting-edge technology to the banking and financial services sector, is seeking a Senior Software Engineer (.NET) to join their backend engineering function.</p><p><br></p><p>This is a senior, hands-on role with a strong focus on backend development, system design, and cloud-native architecture. You will play a key role in shaping scalable, secure, and resilient platforms that support mission-critical financial services.</p><p><br></p><p>The position suits an experienced engineer who combines deep technical expertise with strong communication, stakeholder engagement, and problem-solving skills.</p><p><br></p><p>Key Responsibilities</p><ul><li>Lead the design, development, and evolution of backend services using modern .NET technologies</li><li>Collaborate closely with technical and business stakeholders to shape solution design and delivery</li><li>Build secure, scalable, and high-performance microservices and APIs</li><li>Contribute to architectural decisions, including event-driven and cloud-native approaches</li><li>Champion test automation, code quality, and engineering best practices</li><li>Monitor application performance and drive continuous improvement</li><li>Support incident resolution and contribute to operational stability</li><li>Evaluate and promote the adoption of new tools and technologies where appropriate</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Required Experience & Skills</p><ul><li>Extensive commercial experience with .NET / C# (senior level)</li><li>Strong background in software architecture and system design</li><li>Proven experience building and implementing microservices and APIs</li><li>Hands-on experience with containerisation</li><li>Deep understanding of test automation frameworks and practices</li><li>Strong experience with Microsoft Azure, including modern cloud-native services (e.g. Functions, Cosmos DB, Event Grid)</li><li>Experience designing secure, resilient, and scalable platforms, ideally in regulated environments</li></ul><p><br></p><p>You’ll work with modern .NET and Azure technologies, contribute at architectural level, and have the flexibility to work remotely—while still collaborating with a highly capable engineering team when it counts.</p><p><br></p><p>£85k to £95k plus benefits</p><p>Remote working (once a month visit to London)</p>",
