   "description": "<strong>Senior QA Engineer</strong><p><strong>Birmingham, B2 5DB | 2 days per week in the office</strong><br><strong>Up to £62,000 | 10% bonus | 8% employer pension contribution</strong></p><p>VIQU has partnered with an organisation operating within the UK’s low-carbon electricity sector to recruit a <strong>Senior QA Engineer</strong>. This is a hands-on senior position with responsibility for driving testing quality within a Scrum team while mentoring other QA Engineers and strengthening automation practices.</p><p>Visa sponsorship is available.</p><strong>Key Responsibilities of the Senior QA Engineer</strong><p>• Own quality and testing within your Scrum team<br>• Define test strategies, plans and test cases<br>• Design, develop and maintain automated test scripts<br>• Work with the Principal QA Engineer to improve automation frameworks<br>• Integrate automated testing into CI/CD pipelines<br>• Manage defects through investigation, resolution and retesting<br>• Deliver functional, non-functional and regression testing<br>• Support performance, load, security, accessibility and usability testing<br>• Maintain test environments, data and documentation<br>• Coach and mentor QA Engineers</p><strong>Key Requirements of the Senior QA Engineer</strong><p>• Strong commercial software testing and QA experience<br>• Hands-on Java and Selenium automation experience<br>• Experience using or designing Page Object Model frameworks<br>• Strong understanding of STLC and SDLC in commercial environments<br>• Functional and non-functional testing experience<br>• Commercial edge-case testing experience<br>• Test planning, test design and execution capability<br>• Experience integrating automated tests into CI/CD<br>• Experience coaching and mentoring QA Engineers<br>• Strong debugging and analytical skills<br>• Willingness to complete BPSS screening</p><p>The <strong>Senior QA Engineer</strong> will receive a salary of up to £62,000, a 10% bonus and an 8% employer pension contribution, with two days per week based in the Birmingham office.</p><p>Apply now to speak with VIQU IT in confidence, or contact Aaron on the VIQU website. Know someone great? Refer them and receive up to £1,000 if successful (terms apply). For more roles, follow @VIQU IT Recruitment on LinkedIn.</p>",
