   "description": "<p><strong>Senior C# Developer (AI-Assisted Development)</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Location: </strong>Norwich (North)</li><li><strong>100% Fully On-Site </strong></li><li><strong>Salary: </strong>£55,000 – £65,000 per annum (Dependent on Experience)</li><li><strong>Employment Type: </strong>Full-time, Permanent - 35 hour week, Mon-Fri</li><li><strong>Sector: </strong>Technology</li></ul><p><strong>About the Company</strong></p><p>My client is a highly successful, specialist software company whose products support their clients on a global basis. They develop mission-critical software and work closely with major industry partners, and are able to offer a stable yet highly innovative environment.</p><p><strong>The Role</strong></p><p>Our client is pioneering the future of software engineering within their sector/field. In this role, AI agents write a significant portion of the primary C# codebase, and they require an experienced Senior Developer to direct, orchestrate, and validate this output.</p><p>You will not just be coding in a corner; you will act as the \"human-in-the-loop\" engineer, ensuring AI-generated components are woven into robust, enterprise-grade logistics systems where absolute reliability is critical.</p><p><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>AI Orchestration & Review:</strong> Direct, monitor, and review the code outputs generated by AI agents.</li><li><strong>Integration & Architecture:</strong> Piece together AI-generated code blocks into cohesive, scalable, and robust software solutions.</li><li><strong>Advanced Debugging & Hand-Coding:</strong> Step in with strong manual coding skills to refactor, optimize, and fix complex logical errors when the AI falls short.</li><li><strong>Rigorous Testing:</strong> Implement a methodical approach to testing and debugging live, high-stakes logistics systems.</li><li><strong>Process Optimization:</strong> Continuously question current workflows and suggest improvements to the AI prompt strategies, tooling, and general codebase.</li><li><strong>Project Management (Upper Salary Band):</strong> Plan, prioritize, and manage project delivery timelines while managing stakeholders alongside your core development duties.</li></ul><p><strong>Essential Criteria:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Commercial Experience: </strong>Minimum 4+ years of professional C# development experience.</li><li><strong>AI Environment Experience: </strong>Minimum 2+ years of experience working actively with AI coding tools, LLMs, or automated code-generation agents.</li><li><strong>Technical Mastery: </strong>Exceptional hand-coding ability with a deep understanding of C# architecture, rather than a passive acceptance of generated outputs.</li><li><strong>QA Mindset: </strong>A highly methodical approach to system integration, debugging, and comprehensive unit/integration testing.</li><li><strong>Soft Skills: </strong>A confident, articulate communicator who is comfortable constructively challenging architectural ideas and proposing innovations.</li><li><strong>Commute: </strong>Full commitment to working on-site daily at the North Norwich office.</li></ul><p><strong>What’s on Offer</strong></p><ul><li>Competitive salary of £55,000 to £65,000 DOE.</li><li>Workplace pension scheme.</li><li>Dedicated on-site parking.</li><li>Clear career progression within a rapidly growing, specialist tech firm.</li><li>The opportunity to work at the absolute forefront of AI-assisted software development in a visible, high-impact role.</li></ul>",
