   "description": "<p><strong>Care Worker - Nursing Household</strong></p><p><strong>Location: </strong>Copelands Care Home (Millisle, County Down, T22 2BZ)</p><p><strong>Salary: </strong>up to £25,234.56 per annum (£13.12 per hour (Days) | £13.48 per hour (Nights))</p><p><strong>Contract Type</strong>: Permanent</p><p><strong>Work Hours</strong>: Contracts available - 18, 24 or 36 hours per week (Day and Night shifts available)</p><p><strong>Closing date:</strong> Thursday 19 Nov 2026 10:00</p><p>Be part of something new. We are excited to be recruiting Care Workers for a new Nursing Household within our award-winning Copelands Care Home. This is a fantastic opportunity to join a dedicated team delivering person-centred care in a unique household model that creates a genuine \"home from home\" environment for older people, including those living with dementia.</p><p><strong>These roles are ready for immediate start, pending pre-employment checks.</strong></p><p><strong>Please note we do not offer sponsorship for these roles.</strong></p><p><strong>About BCM</strong></p><p> BCM’s mission is to provide quality, compassionate support to people at their point of need. We are a registered charity who seek to help people change their own lives, offering hope in spaces marked by isolation and despair. Our support services range right through from the youngest to our eldest. Our ‘mission’ is one inspired by Christian values, delivered to all irrespective of beliefs. Religious commitment is not required from our staff or anyone wishing to benefit from our services.</p><p><br></p><p> BCM is an Equal Opportunities Employer.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Your New Role</strong></p><p> As a Care Worker within our new Nursing Household, you will work as part of a multidisciplinary team providing high-quality, person-centred care to residents. You will support residents with daily living activities, personal care, mobility, mealtimes, social engagement and maintaining independence, while helping to create a warm, welcoming and homely environment.</p><p>You will build meaningful relationships with residents and their families, contribute to care planning, and play an important role in enhancing residents' wellbeing and quality of life.</p><p><strong>What We Can Offer You</strong></p><ul><li>Competitive hourly rates</li><li>Paid breaks</li><li>Free meal on 12-hour shifts</li><li>Paid training and development opportunities</li><li>Paid Access NI check</li><li>Uniform provided</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
