   "description": "<b>Package Description: </b><p><strong>Imagine a career where every day you help someone live a happier, more independent, and fulfilling life.</strong></p><p>Join our New Milton Service as a Support Worker and you can help someone build confidence, independence and joy and enable them to thrive in their community. </p><p>Every day brings something different. Whether it's providing everyday support, enjoying a visit to the local pub, or joining someone on a holiday adventure, each activity is tailored to the individual's interests and aspirations. It's all about helping people make the most of life. </p><strong>For your support, we offer:</strong><ul><li>£13.00 per hour </li><li>Refer a friend bonus (up to £1,000) </li><li>Full training and ongoing support</li><li>Career development opportunities </li><li>Blue Light Card discounts </li><li>Company pension </li><li>A supportive, values-led team </li></ul><strong>We’re looking for:</strong><ul><li>A calm, patient and caring approach with the willingness to learn and build trust</li><li>Strong Communication Skills </li><li>A team player who values consistency </li><li>A Full UK driving licence </li><li>At least 12 months remaining on your right to work in the UK</li><li>Excellent career development opportunities and fully funded training up to QCF Level 5</li></ul><strong>Who you’ll support</strong><p>You’ll be supporting 2 individuals with learning disabilities at our New Milton Service to thrive and live as independently as possible. You’ll help with personal care and daily routines, while building meaningful, lasting connections. From supporting days out in the community to holidays and new experiences, </p><p>You’ll ensure their care is truly person-centred, respecting their choices, promoting their safety and helping them do the things they love most.</p><strong>Your role:</strong><ul><li>Provide person-centred support and personal care </li><li>Encourage activities and meaningful experiences </li><li>Support communication in a way that works for them</li><li>Follow care plans and maintain accurate records </li><li>Promote independence, safety, and wellbeing </li></ul><p>This is more than a job; it’s about building a relationship and making a lasting difference in someone’s life.</p><p><strong>If this sounds like something you’d enjoy, apply today!</strong></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
