   "description": "<p><strong>**Please note that this advertised position, which is part of occupation code 6131 does not meet the UKVI eligibility requirements for a Skilled Worker Visa. The Trust would not be able to issue a Certificate of Sponsorship for this role**</strong></p>\n<p>The rheumatology department is made up of a busy outpatient area and day unit which together provides lifelong patient centred support for those with auto immune and inflammatory diseases.</p>\n<p>The outpatient clinics see over thirty patients per day across a five-day working week. The patients visiting the department will be seeing consultants, registrars and rheumatology specialist nurses for diagnosis and support around a wide range of auto immune and inflammatory diseases.</p>\n<p>The day unit team administer infusions to approximately thirty-five patients per day again across a five-day week, providing a fast paced and dynamic environment.</p>\n<p>This is a fantastic opportunity for an excellent and motivated communicator with the flexibility to work in a fast paced and varied environment. The successful candidate will have ability to step into either the clinic area or day unit to provide the highest quality care. As a team we are keen to develop members of staff to gain skills in venepuncture and cannulation and to support the rheumatology patient's pathway through the service.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>As post holder, your duties will include:</p> <ul> <li>Supporting clinicians within their clinics</li> <li>Assisting nurses and other staff when needed</li> <li>Work as part of the team in a co-operative, professional and constructive manner.</li> <li>Be aware of the patient's needs - emotional, social, physical, and cultural. Respect privacy, dignity and beliefs</li> <li>Performing observations, height, weight and BMI </li> <li>Compliance with infection prevention policies and procedures.</li> <li>Ensure patients are cared for individually, assist with personal care, manual handling and emotional support whilst in our department</li> <li>Always maintain confidentiality</li> <li>Maintaining ward stocks, keeping storerooms organised, keeping clinical areas and equipment clean and tidy, and any other duties as delegated by nursing staff</li> </ul> <p>Please note, you will receive full training as part of the role</p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>Join us at the Norfolk and Norwich University Hospital and be part of a workforce of over 10,000 staff!</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
