   "description": "<p>Join our dynamic Rehabilitation Therapy Service team and help transform lives through sport, fitness, and physical activity.</p> <p></p> <p>We have an exciting opportunity for an enthusiastic and motivated individual with a passion for sport, fitness, and wellbeing to join our dedicated Health &amp; Fitness team at Broadmoor Hospital, one of the UK's leading high-security forensic mental health hospitals.</p> <p></p> <p>Working within a unique and rewarding environment, you will play a key role in supporting patients on their recovery journey through the delivery of engaging fitness, exercise, and physical activity programmes. Working alongside experienced Health &amp; Fitness professionals, you will help design and deliver both group and individual exercise sessions that promote physical health, mental wellbeing, confidence, and social engagement.</p> <p></p> <p>Applicants must hold a minimum <strong>Level 2 Gym Instructor qualification</strong> and be committed to encouraging and motivating individuals experiencing acute and enduring mental health conditions. You will support patients across a range of outstanding facilities, including the main fitness suite, indoor sports hall, fitness studio, ward-based gyms and an outdoor 3G multi-use games area, creating positive opportunities for participation, achievement, and recovery through sport and exercise.</p> <p></p> <p>This is a truly rewarding role for someone who wants to combine their passion for fitness with the opportunity to make a meaningful difference in people's lives every day.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>The Health and Fitness assistant works with other diciplines to activity motivate patients and helps them to engage in physical activities and sports. They will be expected to work as a team member and follow the guidance of senior staff.</p> <p></p> <p>Health and Fitness team offer a weekly programme of activities for patients on every ward in the hospital. There is also a need for all staff in the team to take a role in the department safety procedures, such as daily searches of patients and the environment, preparation work for sessions, undertaking patient observations, escorting patients and helping with the management of patient incompatibilities. </p></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
