   "description": "<strong>Would you like to make a real difference in people's lives and help them remain independent in their own homes?</strong> We are looking for an enthusiastic, compassionate and motivated <strong>Therapy Support Worker</strong> to join our Community Therapy Team in Swadlincote. Working alongside Physiotherapists, Occupational Therapists and other health professionals, you will play a key role in supporting patients to achieve their rehabilitation goals and maximise their independence. This is an exciting opportunity for someone who is passionate about delivering high-quality patient care and enjoys working as part of a multidisciplinary team across community settings. As you develop in DCHS there will also be the opportunity for you to apply for the <strong>Advanced Therapy Support Worker Apprenticeship</strong>. <p>The service provides cover 7 day per week, 08:30-16:30 providing care to our community Therapy patients.</p> <p></p> <p></p> <p></p> <p></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>As a Therapy Support Worker, you will:</p> <ul> <li>Support the delivery of rehabilitation programmes prescribed by registered therapists.</li> <li>Assist patients with therapeutic exercises, mobility practice and activities of daily living.</li> <li>Provide, fit and monitor therapeutic equipment and aids.</li> <li>Monitor and report changes in patients' conditions to the relevant healthcare professional.</li> <li>Communicate effectively with patients, families and members of the multidisciplinary team.</li> <li>Maintain accurate clinical records and contribute to patient reviews.</li> <li>Promote patient independence, wellbeing and recovery.</li> </ul> <p>We are looking for someone who:</p> <ul> <li>Has experience of working with patients or service users in a health, social care or community setting.</li> <li>Demonstrates excellent communication and interpersonal skills.</li> <li>Is compassionate, caring and committed to delivering excellent patient-centred care.</li> <li>Can work both independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team.</li> <li>Has good organisational and time management skills.</li> <li>Is willing to undertake training and develop competencies relevant to the role.</li> <li>Has access to a vehicle for work purposes.</li> </ul> <p>If you are a caring, adaptable and professionally accountable Support worker who wants to make a positive difference in the community, we would welcome your application.</p></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
