   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>Clinical Support Worker Band 3- 24 hours per week</p> <p>We are seeking to recruit a clinical support worker to work in the acute medical unit (AMU) at the Cumberland Infirmary Carlisle. We are a dedicated, diverse, multidisciplinary team providing, providing same day emergency care to patients. We provide care to cardiology, respiratory, renal, gastro, elderly, dementia and frailty patients. We are a busy, ever changing unit, working closely with accident and emergency to provide safe and quality care, supporting a positive journey for patients.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>You must have a caring nature, with excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Essential criteria required for role is to have a care certificate (working towards) will be accepted. The shift pattern is 12.5 hours daily, working weekdays, bank holidays and weekends. Our aim to be paperless, we use symphony data to log patient documentation.</p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>At NCIC, we have an ambition to deliver outstanding healthcare services to the population of North Cumbria. The Trust is committed to creating a centre of excellence in providing rural and remote healthcare and provides a wide range of community and acute services throughout our county.</p>\n<p>Our 5 key principles demonstrate our belief in the delivery of 'safe, high quality care every time':</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Being a clinically led organisation</li>\n<li>Quality and safety at the heart of our Trust</li>\n<li>A positive patient experience every time</li>\n<li>A great place to work</li>\n<li>Managing our money well</li>\n</ul>\n<p>As an organisation we are serious about supporting a diverse workforce that reflects our local community and are very much focused on being an inclusive and compassionate place to work.</p>\n<p>We work as a team within Same Day Emergency care, whilst supporting personal development.</p>\n<p>Across the North East and North Cumbria we are working together to deliver our ambition to be the greenest region in England by 2030. All staff are expected to support sustainability.</p></p> <h4>Details</h4> <h4>Date posted</h4> <p>30 October 2026</p> <h4>Pay scheme</h4> <p>Agenda for change</p> <h4>Band</h4> <p>Band 3</p> <h4>Salary</h4> <p> £25,760 to £27,476 a year Per Annum - Pro Rata </p> <h4>Contract</h4> <p>Permanent</p> <h4>Working pattern</h4> <p> Part-time </p> <h4>Reference number</h4> <p>262-A-26-8385660</p> <h4>Job locations</h4> <p>Acute Medical Unit Cumberland Infirmary</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
