   "description": "<p>The Macmillan Health Care Team provide a robust and consistent package of care for end of life patients and their families seven days a week over 24 hours. The service can also include night sits.</p> <p>The Healthcare Support Worker will assist the registered nurse in the delivery of care to patients within the clinical area.</p> <p>The post holder will work under indirect supervision of the registered nurse and will undertake tasks and duties delegated to them, which are within the scope of this job description. They will work collaboratively within the clinical area to meet the needs of patients and their families, following Group policies and procedures.</p> <p>The role is primarily to support the registered nurse to deliver safe, high quality patient care by undertaking essential hygiene tasks, pressure area care, support to patients with nutrition, hydration, mobility, incorporating prevention of falls and toileting.</p> <p>The Healthcare Support Worker is a valued member of the multidisciplinary team promoting safe and quality care at all times.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><ul> <li>Provide overnight care and support to patients under the direction and supervision of the Registered Nurse.</li> <li>Monitor patients' comfort, wellbeing and safety, reporting any changes in their condition promptly to the Registered Nurse.</li> <li>Assist patients with personal care, toileting, mobility, repositioning and other daily living needs while maintaining dignity and privacy.</li> <li>Support the Registered Nurse with patient observations, routine care and other delegated clinical duties within the scope of competence.</li> <li>Maintain accurate patient records, care notes and other relevant documentation.</li> <li>Answer incoming telephone calls professionally, take messages and direct enquiries to the appropriate staff members.</li> <li>Carry out administrative duties, including updating records, completing paperwork and supporting the smooth running of the service overnight.</li> <li>Drive as required to support patient visits, transport staff or attend other work-related duties, ensuring safe and responsible driving.</li> <li>Maintain confidentiality and adhere to safeguarding, infection prevention and control, health and safety policies.</li> <li>Respond promptly to emergencies, escalating concerns to the Registered Nurse and following relevant procedures.</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
