   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p><strong>Care Support Worker (Children's Residential Care)</strong></p><p><strong>Make Every Day Matter</strong></p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Much Hadham, Hertfordshire<br><strong>Salary:</strong> £13.30 - £14.14 per hour (£25,943 - £27,564 per annum)<br><strong>Hours:</strong> Full-time and Part-time opportunities available<br><strong>Shifts:</strong> Earlies (7.00am-2.30pm) | Lates (2.15pm-9.45pm) | Alternate weekends</p><p><strong>Looking for a career that's rewarding, meaningful and full of opportunity?</strong></p><p><strong>The perfect role if you're interested in:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Childcare</p></li><li><p>Education and Teaching</p></li><li><p>Nursing</p></li><li><p>Psychology</p></li><li><p>Social Work</p></li><li><p>Healthcare</p></li><li><p>Special Educational Needs (SEND)</p></li></ul><p>Whether you're starting your first role in care, looking for a career change, or hoping to gain experience for a future in nursing, teaching, social work or healthcare, we'll provide all the training and support you need to succeed.</p><p><strong>Why join us?</strong></p><p>At St Elizabeth's, you're not just joining a workplace. You're becoming part of a supportive community where you'll feel valued, encouraged and empowered to grow.</p><p>Here, your work has a real impact every single day.</p><p><strong>What you'll be doing</strong></p><p>At St Elizabeth's Centre, no two days are ever the same.</p><p>One day you could be helping a young person conquer their fear of the swimming pool. The next, you might be baking cakes, supporting a trip out with friends, celebrating a personal achievement, or helping someone learn a new life skill. As a Care Support Worker, you'll play a vital role in helping children and young people with epilepsy and complex needs live happy, fulfilling lives while building a rewarding career for yourself.</p><p>Working within our children's residential homes, you'll support children and young people aged 5-19 with epilepsy and complex medical and developmental needs.</p><p>You'll help children to:</p><ul><li><p>Build confidence and independence</p></li><li><p>Develop life skills and reach personal goals</p></li><li><p>Take part in education, therapy and recreational activities</p></li><li><p>Enjoy hobbies, trips out, swimming, baking and community activities</p></li><li><p>Maintain their wellbeing through person-centred care and support</p></li></ul><p>You'll also:</p><ul><li><p>Support daily routines and personal care</p></li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
