   "description": "<strong>Veterinary Patient Care Assistant</strong><strong>CRES SA0053</strong><strong>Veterinary Patient Care Assistant</strong><ul><li><p>On Site</p></li><li><p>The Crescent, Melton Mowbray, Leicestershire, United Kingdom, LE13 0NF</p></li><li><p>First Opinion</p></li><li><p>Fixed Term Contract</p></li><li><p>Crescent SA (Melton Mowbray)</p></li><li><p>Salary will be paid at the National Minimum Wage</p></li></ul><p>Are you ready to put pets first? Join our team as our new <strong>Veterinary Patient Care Assistant.</strong></p><p>At <strong>The Crescent Veterinary Centre,</strong> we make pets a priority every day!</p><p><strong>Role Details:</strong></p><p><strong>Location:</strong> The Crescent, Melton Mowbray, Leicestershire, LE13 0NF</p><p><strong>Contract:</strong> 6-Month Fixed Term Contract - to start December 2026</p><p><strong>Hours:</strong> Full-time, 40 hours per week</p><p><strong>Shift Pattern:</strong> Monday - Friday only, between the hours of </p><p><strong>Salary</strong> : Will be paid at the National Minimum Wage and will be dependent on age</p><p><strong>Discover Our Practice:</strong></p><p>Get a glimpse of what makes us special: The Crescent Veterinary Centre | CVS Vets</p><p><strong>About CVS Vets:</strong></p><p>Joining a CVS Vets-owned practice is more than just starting a job-it's the beginning of a rewarding career with one of the UK's leading veterinary groups.</p><p>Our mission is simple yet meaningful: to provide the best possible care for animals, and this dedication guides everything we do.</p><p>With a network of over 500 practices and more than 8,000 devoted professionals, you'll become part of a supportive community focused on one goal: putting pets first.</p><p><strong>It's in our nature - to care, to support, to learn and to progress. That's what sets us apart at CVS Vets.</strong></p><p><strong>About the role:</strong></p><p>The Patient Care Assistant position is crucial in any veterinary practice. You'll support our skilled RVN's and Vets in providing exceptional care to our animal patients.</p><p>Your responsibilities will include:</p><ul><li>Providing nursing care to our patients</li><li>Assisting Vets and Nurses with animal restraint</li><li>Walking, feeding, and cleaning patients</li><li>Preparing emergency and operating facilities</li><li>Performing general cleaning and maintenance</li><li>Running internal lab samples</li><li>Answering emergency calls</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
