   "expires": "2026-11-05",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>An exciting opportunity has arisen for a Band 2 Healthcare Support Worker to join the Discharge Lounge at the Rehabilitation Unit, Wrexham Maelor Hospital.</p> <p>The discharge lounge is a dedicated area where medically cleared patients wait comfortably for final discharge steps--such as paperwork, medications, transport, or clinical reviews--while freeing inpatient beds and improving hospital throughput. It typically offers recliners, refreshments, nursing support, and proximity to exits for efficient pickup.</p> <p>The Discharge Lounge is open from 7:30 am to 8:00 pm every day. It provides a safe and comfortable environment for you to wait in, while receiving any ongoing care you need.</p> <p>The successful applicant must have excellent communication and organisational skills and have the ability to deliver the highest standards of care in a demanding environment.</p> <p>The ability to speak Welsh is desirable for this post; Welsh and/or English speakers are equally welcome to apply.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>Applicants will work as part of the Nursing Team with the department and undertake patient fundamentals of tasks under the direct or indirect supervision of a Registered Nurse responsible for the patient's management.</p>\n<p>You will need to be flexible and dynamic in your approach in delivering care to patients. The post holder needs to have good communication skills and be an effective team player.</p>\n<p>The ability to speak Welsh is desirable for this post; Welsh and/or English speakers are equally welcome to apply.</p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>If you relish a challenge, have a passion to help others or simply fancy a fresh start, then Betsi Cadwaladr University Health Board (BCUHB) North Wales, has all the right ingredients. The largest health organisation in Wales, providing a full range of primary, community, mental health, acute and elective hospital services for a population of around 700,000, across North Wales . Join our team and get the support you need, in line with our Organisational Values and 'Proud to Lead' competence framework.</p>\n<p>Enjoy being part of working with engaged leadership at all levels, and be assured we are committed to promoting equality and diversity, and are proud to welcome applicants under the \"Disability Confident Employer\" scheme.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
