   "description": "<p><strong>Your Role:</strong></p><p>We are looking for a reliable and motivated individual to join our team as a Healthcare Assistant in our busy dialysis unit.</p><p>Cardiff North Dialysis Unit is a dynamic 32 station unit providing haemodialysis treatment for 128 patients in partnership with the NHS Trust.</p><p>You will help keep the unit running smoothly by managing stock and supplies, supporting housekeeping tasks, and preparing the clinical area ready for patients attending their dialysis treatment.</p><p> </p><p>This is a hands-on, rewarding role in a fast-paced environment. Whether you have previous experience or new to healthcare, well provide the training and support you need to succeed!</p><p><strong>Key Details:</strong></p><p><strong>Location: </strong>Cardiff North Renal Dialysis Unit, Unit C3 Avenue Industrial Estate, Croescadarn Close, Pentwyn, CF23 8HE. Free parking available on site.</p><p><strong>Working hours</strong>: 37.5 hours per week. Monday to Saturday on a rolling rota. <strong>No Sunday or night shifts!</strong>3 x 11.5hour shifts per week plus an additional top up shift every 4 weeks.Long Day = 06:45 18:15 </p><p> </p><p><strong>Salary:</strong> £25,652</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p><strong>Your main responsibilities:</strong></p><ul> <li>Provide general assistance to nursing staff with patient care in the treatment room.</li> <li>Liaise with transport and other departments in order to arrange appointments.</li> <li>Support the unit routine, by escorting patients to the wards, blood specimens and pharmacy errands.</li> <li>Monitor and record patients weights pre and post dialysis.</li> <li>Prepare and serve patients with refreshments.</li> <li>Preparation of the clinical area.</li> <li>Maintain stocks and supplies within the treatment areas.</li> <li>Undertake housekeeping duties.</li> </ul><p><strong>What you need to succeed:</strong></p><ul> <li>Team player with the ability to work unsupervised using your own initiative.</li> <li>Willingness to learn.</li> <li>Good communication skills.</li> <li>Able to demonstrate empathy and sympathy.</li> <li>Be detail focused with the ability to meet daily deadlines.</li> <li>Flexible to cover the needs of the patients/unit.</li></ul></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p><strong>What you get in return</strong></p><p></p><ul><li>27 days annual leave plus 8 bank holidays</li><li>7% employer pension contribution</li><li>Paid breaks</li><li>Enhancements payable for unsocial hours</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
