   "description": "<p>Were looking for someone enthusiastic and dedicated to join our friendly, supportive, and forward-thinking nursing teams. Together, were committed to delivering the highest standards of care and creating the best possible experience for our patients, their families, and carers.</p><p>We have roles available across the Trust and in a variety of specialties including (but not limited to) Critical Care, Theatres and Emergency Medicine. If you are interested in working in a new specialty area you will be supported through a development pathway.</p>Main duties of the job<p>In this role, you will be part of a close-knit team of skilled professionals where patient care is always our top priority. You will be supported, valued, and encouraged to bring your ideas and initiative to a role that is both rewarding and challenging.</p><p>What you can expect:</p><ul><li>A welcoming and supportive team environment</li><li>The opportunity to make a meaningful impact on patients lives</li><li>A role where teamwork, compassion, and communication truly matter.</li></ul></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>As a Health Care Assistant you will support the delivery of high-quality patient care under the supervision of a Registered Nurse. Key responsibilities include:</p><ul><li>Assisting with the assessment, planning, delivery and evaluation of patient care.</li><li>Supporting patients with daily living activities, maintaining their dignity, privacy and wellbeing.</li><li>Monitoring patients' condition through observations and reporting any changes or concerns to senior staff.</li><li>Communicating effectively with patients, families, carers and the multidisciplinary team, maintaining accurate and confidential records.</li><li>Organising and prioritising own workload to meet patient care needs.</li><li>Using healthcare equipment and technology safely to monitor and support patient treatment.</li><li>Following Trust policies, procedures and clinical protocols, including responding appropriately in emergency situations.</li><li>Contributing to service improvement, quality standards, audits and the safe use of resources.</li><li>Maintaining own professional development and supporting the learning and development of junior staff where required.</li><li>Promoting a safe working environment and demonstrating flexibility to meet service demands, including unsocial hours where necessary.</li></ul></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
