   "description": "<p>An exciting opportunity has arisen for 2 practitioners to join the Isle of Wight 0-19 Service as Public Health Nursing Assistants (PHNAs)</p><p>PHNAs are key members of the School Nursing Team. They deliver the National Child Measurement Programme (NCMP), complete hearing and vision screening and identify health needs in new school entrants. PHNAs also deliver health promotion sessions.</p><p>Working under the guidance of Specialist Community Public Health Nurses (School Nurses), they collaborate closely with schools, children, families, carers, and other professionals to improve health outcomes. The role focuses on supporting the health and wellbeing of school-age population while contributing positively to the experience of children and families using the service.</p><p>We are looking for someone who:</p><ul><li>Has an NVQ3 in healthcare or nursery nursing or equivalent</li><li>Has excellent communication and interpersonal skills.</li><li>Enjoys working with children, young people and families.</li><li>Is organised, reliable and able to work as part of a team.</li><li>Has good computer skills and experience of Excel</li><li>Values equality, inclusion and culturally sensitive practice.</li><li>Has a passion for improving public health and wellbeing.</li><li>A full driving licence and use of a car</li></ul><p>This is a rewarding opportunity to make a real difference to the lives and children and their families on the Isle of Wight</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>To undertake the screening of children in Reception year and in Year 6 in line with the National Child Measurement Programme (NCMP) and The Healthy Child Programme (5-19)</p><p>Deliver a universal hearing screening check in line with the UK National Screening Committee recommendations &quot;hearing child&quot;</p><p>Deliver a universal vision screening check in line with the UK National Screening Committee recommendations &quot;vision defects and the national service specification for child vision screening&quot;</p><p>To work with schools to ensure that data collection via the NCMP includes the contact details of parents/carers to enable the weight management service to contact and follow up with parents of children above or below a healthy weight.</p><p>To send individual NCMP letters to support children and families in achieving a healthy weight.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
