   "description": "<p><strong>Support Worker - Flexible Day & Night Shifts</strong></p> <p><strong>Location:</strong> Ringstead, Kettering (NN14)<br><strong>Contract:</strong> Part-Time / Ad Hoc Shifts<br><strong>Shifts:</strong> 8am-8pm (Days) | 8pm-8am (Nights)</p> <p>Brook Street Social Care is recruiting compassionate and reliable <strong>Support Workers</strong> for a friendly residential care home in Ringstead, near Kettering.</p> <p>Are you looking for flexible shifts that fit around your lifestyle? This is a fantastic opportunity to join a supportive team and make a real difference in residents' lives.</p> <p><strong>Your Responsibilities</strong></p> <ul> <li>Supporting residents with personal care and daily living activities.</li><li>Promoting independence, dignity and wellbeing.</li><li>Providing companionship and emotional support.</li><li>Assisting with meals, hydration and mobility.</li><li>Following care plans and safeguarding procedures.</li><li>Working alongside colleagues to deliver high-quality care.</li></ul> <p><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p> <ul> <li>A caring, compassionate and reliable individual.</li><li>Good communication and teamwork skills.</li><li>Previous care experience desirable but not essential.</li><li>Flexibility to work day or night shifts.</li><li>Ideally a driver with access to a vehicle, or someone who can reliably travel to Ringstead.</li></ul> <p><strong>What We Offer</strong></p> <ul> <li>Flexible part-time and ad hoc shifts.</li><li>Day and night opportunities.</li><li>Friendly, supportive working environment.</li><li><strong>No lone working</strong> - you'll always work alongside other team members.</li><li>Ongoing training and development opportunities.</li></ul> <p><strong>Interested?</strong></p> <p>If you're passionate about supporting others and looking for flexible care work in Ringstead, we'd love to hear from you.</p> <p><strong>Apply today with your updated CV, and Sophie at Brook Street Social Care will be in touch!</strong></p>",
