   "posted": "2026-10-28",
   "expires": "2026-11-08",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>We are pleased to offer exciting and rewarding opportunities for compassionate and caring individuals to join our Forensic Inpatient Services across Hampshire as Healthcare Support Workers.</p><p>This role will offer you the opportunity to provide career-defining training and challenges; it will offer exposure to a unique and rewarding environment where you will be part of a close-knit team.</p><p>We have opportunities available at the below inpatient units:</p><ul><li><strong>Ravenswood House</strong> (based in Fareham): a medium and low secure, forensic unit providing assessment, care and treatment for adult men with serious mental illness.</li><li><strong>Southfield </strong>(based in Calmore, Tatchbury Mount-near Southampton): a low secure, forensic mental health inpatient service for people with serious mental illness who are aged 18-65 years.</li><li><strong>Ashford</strong>( also at Tatchbury) is a purpose-built 10-bedded ward specifically for adult men with a learning disability who have been detained under the Mental Health Act.</li></ul><p>If you have excellent team working skills, a patient focused mindset and align with our Trust CARE values, Apply Today!</p><p>Find out more about our Forensic Services here: <em>https://hiowhealthcare.nhs.uk/our-services/a-z-list-of-services/specialist-and-forensic-mental-health</em> (copy and paste the link in to your browser)</p><p><em><strong>These roles benefit from an additional forensic lead payment of £1401 pro rata, per annum.</strong></em></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p><strong>What is the role of a Healthcare Support Worker in a forensic inpatient environment?</strong></p><p>Healthcare Support Workers work closely with service users, their families, friends, and carers. You will be essential in ensuring those who use our services have a positive experience and work as part of our dedicated multi-disciplinary team comprising Nurses, Healthcare Support Workers, Social Workers, Occupational Therapists, Psychologists, Specialist Therapists, and Psychiatrists.</p><p>You will work with other team members to promote independence, by providing effective treatment and skills training within a risk management plan to enable our patients to be discharged into the community, or where needs dictate, onto an appropriate continuing healthcare service.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
