   "description": "<p>We are looking for caring, motivated and enthusiastic Healthcare Support Workers to join our Enhanced Recovery Service.</p><p>Working as part of a multidisciplinary team, you will support people in their own homes following illness, injury or hospital admission to regain confidence, maximise independence and achieve their personal goals. You will provide practical reablement support, encouraging individuals to develop daily living skills and maintain their independence wherever possible.</p><p>You will work closely with patients, families, carers and health and social care colleagues to deliver person-centred care that focuses on what matters most to the individual. The role requires good communication skills, a compassionate approach and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team.</p><p>This is a rewarding opportunity to make a real difference to people's lives by helping them remain independent in their own homes and reducing the need for ongoing support.</p><p>In return, we offer a supportive working environment, regular supervision and opportunities for training and development.</p><p><strong>At present, the Trust is unable to offer Skilled Worker visa sponsorship for this post. Applicants must have the right to work in the UK at the time of application.</strong></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>*The purpose of this role is to support the delivery of responsive, high quality and community based care that enables people to remain safely in their own homes and avoid unnecessary hospital admission.</p><p>*The post holder will contribute to an intermediate care service that supports timely discharge from hospital and promotes rehabilitation, reablement and recovery.</p><p>*The post holder will provide person centred reablement support in line with individual care plans, helping people to regain independence and achieve their personal goals.</p><p>*Care will be delivered in accordance with HIOWH polices, procedures and guidelines, ensuing safe, compassionate and effective practice at all times.</p><p>*Will communicate on a regular basis with the patients, their relatives and colleagues in a caring, compassionate and professional manner using a trauma informed approach.</p><p>*Provide support to the nurse in charge and/or the person responsible for the Clinical care of the patient</p><p>*Exchange factual information with patients using tact, reassurance, empathy, compassion and acknowledging barriers to understanding.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
