   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>We have an exciting opportunity for a motivated Health Care Support Worker to join our Childrens Outpatient Team.</p><p>This post will be predominantly based at University Hospital of North Durham but travel to other sites is required. Our team supports around 32,000 appointments per year so this is a busy role where no two days are the same. There are two vacant roles , one is for 26.25 hours; 8.15am-5.30pm shifts Monday-Friday to meet the needs of the service. One is for a 22 hour post.</p><p>You will be welcoming children and families to the department, supporting Consultant and Nurse led clinics, performing clinical observations and supporting our nursing team with investigations and procedures. You will be expected to take bloods after appropriate training. As well as being a great team player, were looking for someone who is flexible, has initiative and excellent communication skills and will take pride in ensuring the department is maintained to a high standard.</p><p>This is a Trustwide role so whilst you'll be predominantly based at UHND , you will be required to travel to Darlington Memorial, Bishop Auckland, Chester-le-Street Hospitals and Stanley Primary Care centre; you must be able to travel independently across site.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>You will be welcoming children and families to the department, supporting Consultant and Nurse led clinics, performing clinical observations and supporting our nursing team with investigations and procedures. You will be expected to take bloods after appropriate training. As well as being a great team player, were looking for someone who is flexible, has initiative and excellent communication skills and will take pride in ensuring the department is maintained to a high standard</p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>If you are being interviewed you must accept an interview slot in the system to continue, even if you have arranged with the manager.</p><p>You must be able to produce <strong>ALL </strong>certificates stated essential in the person specification or you will not be able to complete pre-employment checks.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
