   "id": "nhse-C9152-26-1173",
   "title": "Mental Health Support Worker",
   "company": "Dorset HealthCare University NHS Foundation Trust",
   "employerType": "Direct",
   "level": "Care",
   "careKind": "Healthcare assistant",
   "nhs": "England",
   "location": "Bournemouth, England",
   "region": "England",
   "postcode": "BH4 8EP",
   "workingOption": "onsite",
   "contract": "Permanent",
   "fullTime": true,
   "salaryFrom": 25760,
   "salaryTo": 27476,
   "salaryText": "£25,760 to £27,476 a year p.a. / pro rata for part time",
   "band": "Band 3",
   "posted": "2026-10-28",
   "expires": "2026-11-11",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>Are you a caring individual looking to join a multi-skilled team and be supported in developing your career with Children and Young People?</p> <p>CAMHS has expanded! The 8-bed inpatient High Intensity Environment/PICU at Alumhurst Road, Bournemouth, is a brand-new state of the art building, designed with input from young people and their families who directly benefit from the facilities.</p> <p>As a Mental Health Support Worker, you will provide exceptional care to young people aged between 13 and 18 years experiencing complex mental health. You will have strong communication skills and be compassionate. You will assist in organised activities, contribute to creating a safe and supportive environment and offer emotional support. Previous experience in healthcare is desirable but not essential.</p> <p><strong>Driving is desirable for this role as there could be a requirement to transport young people to their homes, placements, activities or medical appointments.</strong></p> <p>This is a full-time role; part-time applicants welcome with a minimum of 22.5 hours per week. You will be required to work a range of flexible shifts with weekends/nights at enhanced pay! This can be discussed at interview stage.For any queries, please contact us viadhc.careers@nhs.net</p> <p><strong>Interview date is Friday, 20th November, which will be held as an Assessment Day. Please note, this will be a face-to-face only interview, and you will be required to be available all day.</strong></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p><strong>Shift patterns:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Early - 07.00 to 15.00</li> <li>Late - 12.00 to 20.00</li> <li>Twilight - 16.00 to 00.00</li> <li>Nights - (enhanced pay) - 19:30 to 07.30</li> <li>Long days - 07.00 - 20.00</li> </ul> <p>For further information, regarding the new CAMHS PICU site Join our CAMHS PICU team :: Careers Dorset</p> <p>You will be part of an innovative and forward-thinking team and make a real impact on the lives of young people.</p> <p>You will have the opportunity to attend training courses and participate in personal development training as identified by the line manager.</p> <p>Make accurate records of patient observations, including data entry to the RiO patient records computer system. You will report any complaints by young people, families and carers to the trained staff on duty.</p> <p>Other duties appropriate to the role which may be requested from time to time by the nurse in charge.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
