   "expires": "2026-11-11",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>An exciting opportunity has arisen for a compassionate, motivated, and organised Metastatic Breast Cancer Support Worker to join the team at Blackpool Teaching Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust.</p>\n<p>The successful post holder will play a vital role in supporting patients living with metastatic breast cancer throughout their cancer journey. Working closely with CNS, consultants, allied health professionals, primary care teams, and wider cancer services, you will act as a key point of contact for patients and their families, helping to coordinate care, provide information and support, and ensure individual needs are identified and addressed.</p>\n<p>The role will involve undertaking holistic needs assessments, supporting personalised care planning, coordinating follow-up appointments and investigations, signposting patients to relevant support services, and helping patients navigate complex healthcare pathways. You will be expected to provide practical and emotional support while ensuring patients receive timely access to information, treatment, and services.</p>\n<p>As part of the wider cancer services team, you will contribute to the delivery of high-quality, patient-centred care that improves the experience and outcomes for individuals living with incurable breast cancer. You will be passionate about providing excellent care, have excellent communication and organisational skills, and be able to work effectively both independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team.</p>\n<p></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>The Metastatic Breast Cancer Support Worker will work as an integral member of the Breast Care Nursing Team, providing personalised support and care coordination for patients living with metastatic breast cancer.</p>\n<p>The post holder will:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Act as a dedicated key worker and first point of contact for patients and their families</li>\n<li>Work closely with the Breast Clinical Nurse Specialists, consultants, oncology teams, palliative care services and wider multidisciplinary team to ensure seamless, coordinated care.</li>\n<li>Undertake and document Holistic Needs Assessments and assist patients in developing personalised care and support plans.</li>\n<li>Support the delivery of personalised cancer care</li>\n<li>Coordinate follow-up appointments, investigations, referrals and patient reviews .</li>\n<li>Signpost patients to relevant services</li>\n<li>Identify patients who may require additional support and escalate to the CNS</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
