   "posted": "2026-10-28",
   "expires": "2026-11-03",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>Do you want to make a difference to people's lives?</p>\n<p>We are looking for individuals with or without experience to work in healthcare, to join the NHS family helping people from your local community. Healthcare Support Worker opportunities are available in Orsett Ward.</p>\n<p>No experience? No problem. We will teach you everything you need to know. It is more important that you are a caring and kind, with a genuine desire to help and support patients and their families. If this sounds like you, then you already have the skills that make a great Health Care Support Worker.</p>\n<p>Right from the time you join us, you will have access to learning, development and training opportunities. As you progress in your NHS career you will acquire the knowledge, skills and confidence you need to provide safe and compassionate patient care.</p>\n<p>Mid and South Essex is a great place to work, offering a working environment with an inclusive culture that looks after and values our people and creates a sense of belonging. We encourage applications from people who embrace our values and who will enable us to expand our diverse workforce.</p>\n<p>The Healthcare Support Worker role can also lead to a range of career opportunities. With the right support, those who want to can undertake necessary training to become our future nurses, nursing associates and midwives.</p>\n<p><strong>No VISA sponsorship available for this role</strong></p>\n<p>Please note that we reserve the right to close this vacancy early if we receive a suitable number of applications.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>As a Healthcare Assistant you will play a vital role in supporting our Nursing and Midwifery teams to deliver high-quality, compassionate care to patients. Each day will be varied, and you'll work as part of a dedicated team to provide practical and emotional support to patients and their families.</p> <p><strong>Your duties may include:</strong></p> <p>Assisting patients with personal care, including washing, dressing, and toileting</p> <p>Supporting patients with mobility and helping them move safely and comfortably</p> <p>Serving meals and assisting patients with eating and drinking</p> <p>Making and changing beds, ensuring a clean and comfortable environment</p> <p>Engaging with patients and their families, offering reassurance and support</p> <p>Monitoring and reporting changes in a patient's condition to the nursing team</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
