   "expires": "2026-11-11",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p> An exciting opportunity has arisen for a Band 3 Clinical Support Worker post within the Paediatric Acute Service at Forth Valley Royal Hospital. The unit consists of a 25 bedded inpatient ward, an 8 bedded Paediatric Daycare Unit and a Paediatric Outpatient Department. </p><p> This role is to assist & support the nursing staff in caring for sick children & their families </p><p> The successful candidate will be a keen team player, have excellent communication skills and display an enthusiasm to promote person centered and family centered care within our Paediatric Acute Service. The post may involve internal rotation to night duty. </p><p> For further information and informal enquiries please contact Deborah Colvin, Senior Charge Nurse on 01324 567199/567203. </p><p> The duties of this post require the successful candidate to be a member of the Protecting Vulnerable Groups (PVG) Scheme. More information on this scheme can be found at www.disclosurescotland.co.uk </p><p> <b> Certificate of Sponsorship </b> </p><p> Applicants who require sponsorship to work in the UK are advised to carefully review the eligibility criteria for the Skilled Worker or Health and Care Worker visa routes. NHS Forth Valley may be able to offer sponsorship for certain roles, provided the post meets the minimum salary threshold and any other required criteria. If you are currently working in the UK on a Skilled Worker visa, transitional arrangements may apply. Please note that sponsorship is not guaranteed and is assessed on a case-by-case basis following interview and at the commencement of pre-employment checks. For further information on visa requirements and sponsorship eligibility, please refer to the UK Government guidance . </p><p> It is also recommend that anyone applying for health and social care jobs in the UK from abroad read the following guidance: Applying for health and social care jobs in the UK from abroad - GOV.UK (www.gov.uk) </p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
