   "salaryText": "£26,813 to £27,890 a year per annum pro rata",
   "band": "Band 3",
   "posted": "2026-10-27",
   "expires": "2026-11-03",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>An exciting opportunity has arisen for an experienced, enthusiastic and highly motivated Band 3 Nursing Support Worker (Primary Care) to join our friendly and supportive team at Bryntirion Surgery, Bargoed. The post is for 30 hours per week, working over 5 days.</p>\n<p>We are looking for staff who have energy, enthusiasm, commitment and drive and who are patient-centred.</p>\n<p>You will have the opportunity to work as part of a multidisciplinary team, delivering care to patients within a Primary Care setting, under supervision provided by a registered healthcare professional.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><ul> <li>Plan and prioritise own delegated workload, ensuring tasks are completed efficiently, safely and effectively, using your initiative to prioritise the work based on the needs of patients, adjusting to ensure emergencies and priority tasks are completed to deadlines.</li> <li>Work within established procedures when delivering care; and under the supervision of a registered healthcare professional.</li> <li>Record accurate and timely information in the appropriate documentation including documenting for example, height, weight, BMI</li> <li>Support registered health professional in the delivery of chronic disease and other clinics as required</li> <li>Undertake and record physiological measurements which may vary depending on the speciality for example, temperature, blood pressure, respiration rate, pulse and diabetic foot checks, escalating all abnormal findings to the registered healthcare professional</li> <li>Undertake Point of Care testing, for example carrying out urinalysis including pregnancy testing, and escalating anyabnormalities, recording blood glucose, including conducting compliance with both internal and external quality assessment of equipment.These clinical duties are not exhaustive and the Nursing Support Worker may be required to attend further study to develop new skills.</li> </ul></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>Aneurin Bevan University Health Board (ABUHB) is a multi-award-winning NHS organisation serving the communities of Gwent. With more than 14,000 staff and volunteers, we provide safe, high-quality, and compassionate care across hospitals, GP practices, community services, and mental health settings. As a University Health Board, research, education, and innovation are central to our work, supporting evidence-based practice and continuous improvement.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
