   "description": "<strong>Health Care Support Worker - Band 2 - Female Acute - Heather Ward &amp; 136 Suite - Airedale Centre for Mental Health</strong> <p>Are you a compassionate and motivated Health Care Support Worker looking to make a genuine difference?</p> <p>Join Heather Ward and the Section 136 Suite, supporting women aged 18-65 experiencing acute mental health difficulties.</p> <p>As a Band 2 Health Care Support Worker, you will be at the heart of patient care, building therapeutic relationships and supporting physical, emotional and mental health needs alongside registered healthcare professionals and the wider multidisciplinary team.</p> <p>Every day is different. You may support women experiencing anxiety, depression, psychosis, emotional distress, trauma-related difficulties or mental health crisis, providing compassionate, safe and person-centred care.</p> <p>You may also support women within the Section 136 Suite, helping maintain a calm, safe environment while protecting dignity, privacy and wellbeing.</p> <p>This is a 24-hour service, and the post requires flexibility to work a rota including long days, nights and weekends.</p> <p><strong>Closing Date: 14th November</strong><strong>Shortlisting Date: 16th November</strong></p> <p><strong>Please ensure you are available to attend the in-person Assessment Centre on 21st November before applying. Virtual interviews will not be offered and alternative dates cannot be accommodated.</strong></p> <p><strong><em>This position is not eligible for sponsorship set by the Home Office and the skilled worker visa occupation list.</em></strong></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>Your duties will include:</p> <ul> <li>Providing compassionate, person-centred care while maintaining privacy, dignity and individual choice.</li> <li>Supporting personal care, hygiene, meals and other day-to-day care needs.</li> <li>Building positive therapeutic relationships and communicating effectively with patients, relatives and colleagues.</li> <li>Supporting observations and monitoring patients' physical and mental wellbeing.</li> <li>Recognising, recording and promptly escalating changes or concerns.</li> <li>Supporting admissions, discharges and transitions in care.</li> <li>Maintaining accurate written and electronic records.</li> <li>Supporting women within the Section 136 Suite who may be distressed, anxious, frightened or confused.</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
