   "expires": "2026-11-09",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>The post holder--Band 3 Healthcare Assistant--occupies a pivotal position in delivering high-quality, compassionate, and recovery-oriented care to individuals with complex, acute, chronic, and forensic mental health needs. Under the direct supervision of a Registered Nurse , the post holder is responsible for supporting the implementation of individualised care plans, managing daily clinical priorities within established guidelines, and actively promoting a safe and therapeutic environment.<strong>Mandatory Working Requirements &amp; Genuine Occupational Requirements (GOR)</strong>1. <strong>Full Shift Rotation (Day &amp; Night Duty)</strong>: Owing to the continuous 24/7 care demands of a forensic inpatient ward, the post holder must work a full rotational pattern, including compulsory internal rotation to night shifts, weekends, and bank holidays. This is a fundamental, non-negotiable requirement of the role and is in accordance with the Working Time Regulations 1998.2. <strong>Physical Intervention (PMVA): </strong>Ensuring safety within a forensic environment is a critical aspect of the position. The post holder is required to participate in physical restraint and emergency safety procedures, utilising approved Prevention and Management of Violence and Aggression (PMVA) protocols. Physical fitness, capability, and willingness to undertake, pass, and annually re-certify in mandatory PMVA physical training are essential components of this role.</p></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
