   "expires": "2026-11-09",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p><strong>This vacancy is offering full time and a part time role. The part time role is 30 hours and therefore not eligible for sponsorship. Applicants must have an existing right to work in the UK and be able to maintain that right for the duration of employment without sponsorship from the Trust</strong></p>\n<p>An exciting opportunity has arisen for a dynamic healthcare assistant to work in the Central Lancashire District Nursing Service. </p>\n<p>The successful applicant will be responsible for providing skilled nursing care in a variety of settings, and will be part of an innovative, dynamic district nursing team.</p>\n<p>We are looking for experienced healthcare assistants who are patient and family focused, with excellent communication skills and an interest in community district nursing. If you identify with our patient centred vision of care and enjoy working in partnership with the local community, come and join us.</p>\n<p>You will be offered a robust induction programme tailored to your developmental needs, regular clinical supervision and the opportunity to access a broad range of training opportunities.</p>\n<p>We require flexible, self-motivated individuals, the post is a part-time role covering shifts over a 7 day period between the hours of 07.45 and 22.00</p>\n<p>For further information about the role please contact us using the details provided</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>To work as part of the Integrated Neighbourhood/ Locality team under the direction of the district nursing team leader and manager, supporting the provision of high quality holistic nursing care to patients, 24 hours a day 7 days a week</p>\n<p>The Health Care Assistant will work with and without direct supervision of a registered nurse providing care to patients in their own homes and other community settings, as delegated by the district nursing team leader following appropriate training and supervision to ensure clinical competence and safe effective care</p>\n<p>To support other health care professionals in the provision of high quality care in the locality population</p></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
