   "expires": "2026-11-05",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p><em>Are you a caring and compassionate individual looking to make a difference?</em></p><p>We are seeking enthusiastic and caring <strong>Healthcare Assistants to join our friendly team on East and North Ward at Hinckley and Bosworth Community Hospital,</strong> a nurse-led ward caring for patients requiring end of life care, rehabilitation and medical step down from the acute.</p><p>Working alongside nurses and the wider multidisciplinary team, you will provide high-quality, person-centred care, support patients in their recovery, and promote independence in a supportive and rewarding environment.</p><p><strong>What we're looking for:</strong></p><p></p><ul><li>Experience in Health and/or Social Care.</li><li>A caring, compassionate, and reliable approach.</li><li>Strong communication skills and a team-focused attitude.</li><li>Flexibility with rota shifts - This role covers a 24-hour, 7-day service and shifts are worked on a rota basis.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><p></p><ul><li>A supportive team environment.</li><li>Training and development opportunities, including completion of the Care Certificate where required.</li><li>Flexible working opportunities.</li><li>Free on-site parking.</li><li>NHS Benefits including 27 days holiday plus BH and a generous pension scheme and so much more!</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Important: </strong>Unfortunately, we are unable to offer sponsorship for this role. The minimum contracted hours available are 22.5 hours per week. Please do not apply if you require sponsorship or cannot work the minimum hours.</p><p><strong>For an informal discussion, please contact: Joanne Jackson, Ward sister joanne.jackson36@nhs.net</strong></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p></p><ul><li>Undertaking clinical observations and providing clinical care as delegated.</li><li>Supporting our patients in maintaining their health and well-being.</li><li>Providing personal care to include washing, dressing and toileting / continence care.</li><li>Accurately recording patient information.</li><li>Working collaboratively and co-operatively with others to meet the needs of patients and their families.</li></ul><p></p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>We may close the advert early, if we receive a sufficient number of applicants, so please apply as soon as possible.</p><p><strong>About Us</strong></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
