   "description": "<b>Package Description: </b><p>A career where your kindness could brighten someone's day</p><p>Join our care home team as a Night Care Assistant and make a real difference in residents’ lives while building a rewarding career in care, no experience necessary.</p><p>All you need is compassion and the right to work in the UK. We’ll provide fully funded training and excellent career development to help you grow.</p><p>And the best part? You’ll get just as much back, the gratitude, the stories, the smiles that stay with you, plus:</p><strong>You’ll receive:</strong><ul><li>Outstanding career development with fully funded training and qualifications (up to QCF Level 5)</li><li>Hours to include working alternate weekends</li><li>Days and nights currently available </li><li>Refer-a-Friend scheme – earn up to £1,000*</li><li>Up to £12.91 per hour</li><li>Blue Light Card discounts</li><li>Company pension scheme</li><li>On-demand pay</li></ul><strong>The role of a Care Assistant:</strong><ul><li>Provide high-quality personal care and support to residents.</li><li>Assist with medication administration and recording.</li><li>Support residents with daily living activities and routines.</li><li>Build meaningful relationships and provide companionship.</li><li>Help enrich residents' lives through activities, hobbies, and social engagement.</li><li>Promote residents' dignity, independence, and well-being.</li><li>Work as part of a caring team to deliver outstanding person-centred care</li></ul><p>About you:</p><ul><li>Experience working in a care setting is required for this role </li><li>Compassionate, patient and great with people</li><li>Minimum 12 months right to work in the UK (we cannot currently offer sponsorship)</li><li>This position is working 36 hours per week, to include alternate weekends </li><li>Please note this is a maternity cover position for 12 months </li><li>Please note this is a night shift position</li></ul><p>Whether you’re listening to residents’ wonderful life stories, helping with daily routines, or simply being a friendly face that brightens their day, you’ll be making a real difference to their lives.</p><strong>Where you'll be working:</strong><p>Click here to view the care home: <br>Care Quality Commission Rating: 'Good' </p><p>Apply to be a Care Assistant, where compassion meets purpose.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
