   "description": "<p>**advert may close early due to volume of applications**</p>\n<p>Main Theatres Department</p>\n<p>University Hospital North Tees</p>\n<p> 37.5 hours per week</p>\n<p>Contract Type : full time substantive</p>\n<p>Disclosure Check: ENHANCED</p>\n<p>Would you like to be part of an increasing service delivering high quality care to patients?</p>\n<p>Have you got a caring nature and a willingness to learn and develop new skills in a supported environment?</p>\n<p>We have a vacancy for Band 3 Theatre Support Workers within main theatres.</p>\n<p>You will help provide a high standard of care to patients undergoing anaesthetic and surgical procedures, assisting in the departments workload and delivering a quality service in a professional manner.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>To provide support to the multi professional team by undertaking appropriate duties following assessment and planning of requirements by a registered practitioner. Additionally to provide support by undertaking non nursing and ancillary duties.</p>\n<p>The post holder will work as a member of the multi professional team with supervision/guidance from registered practitioner.</p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p><strong>South Tees Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust and North Tees and Hartlepool NHS Foundation Trust have come together to form University Hospitals Tees. As a result, post holders may be required to work across sites within both organisations.</strong></p> <p><strong></strong></p> <p><strong>Across University Hospitals Tees, our ambition is to be the best place to work, ensuring we have the right staff in the right roles at the right time to deliver outstanding patient care and experience.</strong></p> <p><strong></strong></p> <p><strong>We are committed to supporting our staff through an inclusive and supportive working environment, offering health and wellbeing initiatives, staff benefits, and opportunities for personal and professional development.</strong></p> <p><strong></strong></p> <p><strong>We support the 'Making Every Contact Count' approach to behaviour change in the promotion of health and wellbeing of individuals and communities.</strong></p> <p></p></p> <h4>Details</h4> <h4>Date posted</h4> <p>26 October 2026</p> <h4>Pay scheme</h4> <p>Agenda for change</p> <h4>Band</h4> <p>Band 3</p> <h4>Salary</h4> <p> £25,760 to £27,476 a year pro rata per annum </p> <h4>Contract</h4> <p>Permanent</p> <h4>Working pattern</h4> <p> Full-time </p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
