   "description": "<p><strong>*We are unable to provide Sponsorship for this role*</strong></p> <p>Working within a CAMHS inpatient unit you will bring lived experience to the role and use this to support and mentor the young people on the unit.</p> <p>Your role will involve having regular 1:1 engagement sessions with the young people and helping them to navigate the complexities of their inpatient stay as well as using your experience to support them.</p> <p>You will attend daily multi disciplinary team meetings as well as weekly ward reviews and CPA reviews on an ad hoc basis. During these meetings you will act as a advocate for the young people and bring their voice to the wider MDT.</p> <p>You will support the young people with therapeutic activities and accompany them on trips out alongside other staff members.</p> <p></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>To establish a supportive and respectful relationship with the young people.</p> <p>To work primarily with service users on a 1:1 and in group settings as agreed with team service manager and team leader.</p> <p>To help individuals to identify their own achievable and meaningful recovery goals to compliment the work undertaken by the psychology and nursing teams.</p> <p>Draw upon own lived experience to inspire hope, model self-awareness and facilitate service users in developing their own resourcefulness for managing their health and wellbeing.</p> <p>To feedback any concerns to the nurse in charge or ward manager and to document your interactions with the young people clearly and accurately.</p> <p>To attend multi-disciplinary team meeting and ward reviews and bring the voice of the young person to these meetings.</p> <p></p> <p></p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>Valuing you. Recognising your dedication. At EPUT, we look after you.</p> <ul> <li>Receive supervision and support to help you fulfil your potential.</li> <li>Join an inclusive EPUT community and connect with others through engagement events and equality or champion networks.</li> <li>If you need help, we provide mental health and wellbeing services, occupational health advice and counselling.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Benefits</strong></p> <ul> <li>27 days holiday, plus bank holidays, rising to 33 days after 10 years' service.</li> <li>Excellent pension of up to 14.5% of your pensionable pay.</li> <li>Staff discounts include Blue Light Card, NHS discount offers, and staff benefits.</li> <li>£8K relocation package if you move to Essex to join us</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
