   "description": "Join Our Hospital at Home Team <p>Are you passionate about delivering high-quality, person-centred care to patients in the comfort of their own homes?</p> <p>We have a number of full time and part time Community Support Worker Hospital@Home opportunities available</p> <p><em><strong>Please note: Wye Valley NHS Trust is unable to provide sponsorship for these roles. Dependant visa's requirement: minimum of 12 months remaining prior to expiry.</strong></em></p> <p>Our Hospital at Home service, part of the Unplanned Care Directorate, is expanding in line with the national vision to move appropriate care from acute settings into the community. We provide personalised, proactive care closer to home, enabling patients to receive appropriate acute-level care in their own homes.</p> <p>Hospital at Home is a 24/7 service providing safe, responsive and high-quality care.</p> <p>We are looking for motivated, compassionate individuals to join our Herefordshire Hospital at Home Team as Band 3 Healthcare Support Workers.</p> <p>Staff will work shift patterns, including day and night shifts, weekends and bank holidays, in line with service needs.</p> <p><em>If we receive a large volume of applications, we reserve the right to close this vacancy early.</em></p> <p></p> <p></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><ul> <li>Assist qualified Nursing staff in a range of patient care duties.<strong> </strong></li> <li>To undertake a range of delegated nursing tasks, including cannulation and taking blood or urine samples, carrying out basic wound assessments and applying simple dressings, taking routine observations and supporting clients with medication.<strong> </strong></li> <li>To record patient information.<strong> </strong></li> <li>To provide planned patient care.</li> <li><strong>Requirements:</strong>o A valid, in-date driving licenceo Access to a car for worko <strong>Flexibility to work day and night shifts</strong>o Commitment to completing relevant competencies and training</li> </ul></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>Wye Valley NHS Trust is a member of an NHS Foundation Group with South Warwickshire NHS FT , the George Eliot Hospital NHS Trust and Worcestershire Acute Hospitals NHS Trust.</p> <p>Located on the border with Wales in the shadow of the Black Mountains, we provide acute and community services across Herefordshire and into parts of Powys and run Hereford County Hospital and the community hospitals in Bromyard, Leominster and Ross-on-Wye.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
