   "expires": "2026-11-09",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>Are you passionate about supporting the emotional wellbeing of children and young people? Do you want to be part of a service making a real difference in schools and communities across Leicester, Leicestershire and Rutland?</p><p>Our Mental Health Support Teams (MHSTs) are seeking enthusiastic and compassionate Band 3 Senior Healthcare Assistants to join our growing multidisciplinary team. This is an excellent opportunity to support children, young people and families to access the right help at the right time while developing your skills within an innovative and supportive mental health service.</p><p>As a Senior Healthcare Assistant, you will support the delivery of high-quality mental health care under the supervision of registered practitioners. You will play a key role within our Triage and Duty Service, ensuring referrals are managed efficiently and that children and families receive timely advice, support and access to appropriate services.</p><p>Working as part of an experienced multidisciplinary team, you will:</p><ul><li>Gather information following referral to assess mental health needs.</li><li>Provide mental health advice and signposting.</li><li>Support practitioners with delegated clinical and therapeutic activities.</li><li>Promote positive mental health and wellbeing.</li><li>Respond appropriately to safeguarding concerns.</li><li>Maintain accurate and timely clinical records.</li></ul><p>For an informal discussion, please contact Gemma Billson at gemma.billson@nhs.net</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>Please see the Job Description, Person Specification and Additional Information attached to this Advert.</p><p>We are looking for someone who:</p><p></p><ul><li>Has experience working in a mental health setting.</li><li>Demonstrates excellent communication and interpersonal skills.</li><li>Is compassionate, organised and able to work effectively in a busy service.</li><li>Can build positive relationships with children, young people, families, schools and partner agencies.</li><li>Understands safeguarding and risk management.</li><li>Is committed to improving outcomes for children and young people.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
