   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p><strong>We do not offer sponsorship for these opportunities.</strong></p> <p><strong>Opportunities in Leeds</strong></p> <p>Are you interested in a career in Mental Health or Learning Disabilities Care? </p> <p>Or maybe you are an experienced Health Support Worker looking for your next opportunity... either way, this is a great way to find out more about our services before taking the next step.</p> <p>We are recruiting for passionate and caring Health Support Workers to join various services here at The Leeds and York Partnership NHS Foundation Trust.</p> <p>We are hosting a virtual one-hour information session on Monday the 23rd of November at 12:15 pm, where you can hear directly from our clinical services about what the role looks like on a day to basis.</p> <p>You will have the chance to ask any questions you may have about the job.</p> <p>Simply follow the short and simple application process on this advert, and we will be in touch with you on Monday 16th November to provide details of how you can join the session which will be on -</p> <p><strong>Monday 23rd of November at 12:15 pm</strong></p> <p>If, following the online session, you are interested in being considered for any of the opportunities available, we will provide you with an application link.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p><strong>Services may include:</strong></p> <p><strong>Learning Disabilities, Specialised Supported Living Service - Leeds</strong></p> <p>Provide support for who you are, and who you want to be.</p> <p><strong>Adult Acute Inpatient Services - Leeds</strong></p> <p>Primarily for people of working age who have been assessed via the Crisis Assessment Services as individuals who require assessment and treatment.</p> <p><strong>Older People's Acute Inpatient Services - Leeds</strong></p> <p>Provide care and support for people with acute mental health needs including those with a diagnosis of dementia.</p> <p></p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>The Leeds and York Partnership NHS Foundation Trust (LYPFT) is the main provider of Mental Health and Learning Disability services in Leeds. We also provide specialist inpatient services in York and some highly specialised services across the country. As a teaching trust with strong links to local universities, we are a centre of excellence for teaching, research and development.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
