   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p><strong>This role isnot eligible for visa sponsorship. If it is identified that you require sponsorship to undertake this role your application may be withdrawn</strong></p> <p>An exciting opportunity has arisen to join the Child and Adolescent Mental Health Services (CAMHS) South Team West (STW) Eating Difficulties Service as a Band 3 Health Care Support Worker.</p> <p>This role is ideal for an individual who is passionate about supporting children and young people experiencing eating disorders and associated mental health difficulties. Working within a specialist multidisciplinary team, you will play a vital role in delivering physical health monitoring and supporting the physical wellbeing of young people receiving treatment from the service.</p> <p>You will provide compassionate, person-centred support during physical health assessment appointments, helping young people and their families engage positively with treatment. The role offers the opportunity to develop specialist skills within children's mental health services while contributing to high-quality, recovery-focused care.</p> <p>The post will be based across Severn Fields Health Village and The Telford Langley School, with occasional travel across community settings to meet the needs of young people and the service.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><ul>\n<li>Support young people during their physical health assessment appointments, ensuring that the appointment is therapeutic and supportive using clear communication with the young person and their family. Ensure the use of clear instructions for the tasks needing to be completed.</li>\n<li>Observe, monitor and report any changes in presentation or behaviour during the physical health assessment to senior staff.</li>\n<li>Regularly provides advice and guidance - promoting healthy activities and lifestyle choices.</li>\n<li>Responsible for contribution towards planning and undertaking delivery of planned physical health care observations.</li>\n<li>Contribute to creating a therapeutic and safe environment.</li>\n<li>Participates in Trust audits and surveys, information collection for clinical audits specific to own work area, the implementation of agreed action plans and practice development initiatives as part of the team.</li>\n</ul></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>Come and work with us at our award-winning NHS Trust, leading the way for trying new and better ways of working to help improve life for our local communities.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
