   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p> NHS Scotland is committed to encouraging equality and diversity among our workforce and eliminating unlawful discrimination. The aim is for our workforce to be truly representative and for each employee to feel respected and able to give their best. To this end, NHS Scotland welcomes applications from all sections of society. </p> <p> A new and exciting opportunity has arisen for individuals to join the Ophthalmology Team within the Surgical Directorate, NHS Tayside. </p><p> One post will be primarily based at Perth Royal Infirmary, with a requirement for occasional cross-site working at Ninewells Hospital. The second post will involve regular cross-site working between Ninewells Hospital and Perth Royal Infirmary. </p><p> These roles offer the opportunity to play a key part in delivering high-quality patient care and influencing the patient journey within ophthalmology outpatient services, with a particular focus on the Intravitreal Therapy (IVT) service . </p><p><br></p><p> You must be able to demonstrate a desire to be an integral part of the development of care and services within ophthalmology. </p><p><br></p><p> Applicants must evidence a good standard of basic education and have or be willing to work towards recognised healthcare qualifications i.e. SVQ 11 or equivalent level study in Health Care. </p><p><br></p><p> You will be required to undertake any necessary training, to achieve the mandatory Induction standards for healthcare support Workers in Scotland and to comply with the Code of Conduct throughout your employment. </p><p><br></p><p> Informal enquiries to: </p><p> Specialist Nurse Jennifer Sinclair or Christine Ayre, email: jennnifer.sinclair1@nhs.scot or christine.ayre@nhs.scot </p><p> Tel 01382 660111 ext 32714 </p><p><br></p><p> Hours of work are: 36.0 hours (7-day working may be required to support the service) </p><p><br></p><p> Shortlisted applicants will be contacted by email. Please check your emails regularly, including junk/spam folder. </p><p><br></p> <p> <b> ADDITIONAL INFORMATION FOR CANDIDATES </b> </p><ul><li> You should apply for this post by completing the application process on Jobtrain. </li><li> DO NOT upload a CV as this will not be used for shortlisting purposes. </li><li> Posts close at midnight on the indicated date. </li><li> For help to complete an application on Job Train please follow this link: https://www.careers.nhs.scot/how-to-apply/application-process/ </li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
