   "hourlyFrom": 12.85,
   "hourlyTo": 12.85,
   "salaryText": "£12.85 per hour",
   "posted": "2026-10-23",
   "expires": "2026-12-04",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p><strong>We are looking to recruit warm, flexible, and motivated Female Support Workers to provide person-centred support at our bespoke development in Warwick.</strong></p> <p><strong>Our service is a large, modern building consisting of 15 flats. It provides Supported Living opportunities for people with learning disabilities, physical disabilities, complex needs, and autism. We take pride in offering unique and individualized person-centred active support services that are stimulating, enjoyable, and motivational. Our goal is to help individuals explore life opportunities, build and develop their unique skills, promote choice and independence and achieve what matters most to them.</strong></p> <p><strong>As a Support Worker, you’ll bring a passion for promoting active involvement and communication, ensuring every day is a good day for our service users living in the Warwick area. Every day will be unique, filled with a variety of activities such as baking, listening to music, walking and more.</strong></p> <p><strong>Your responsibilities will include providing respectful personal care and assisting with domestic tasks like cooking and cleaning, engaging with service users to build trusting therapeutic relationships, and encouraging wellbeing and positive coping skills. You will offer support to service users in their own homes or other settings, as part of a structured approach, providing respite to carers, and offering practical and emotional support to families where appropriate.</strong></p> <p><strong>A full UK manual driving licence is an essential requirement of this role. </strong></p> <p><strong>No previous experience required. </strong>We provide all of your training as you begin your new career in care, including the opportunity to work towards earning your QCF Diploma in Health and Social Care. All employees have access to our training system where, through a combination of in person and e-learning courses, you can learn the skills required to develop in your role and progress toward senior roles.</p> <p>Gender is considered to be an occupational requirement – Equality Act 2010.</p> <p><strong>Vacancy Reference Number: 97046</strong></p> <p>Applications for this role must be submitted via the Creative Support website using the above vacancy reference number.</p> <p><strong>Benefits of working with Creative Support include a probationary bonus, pension contributions, 28 days Annual Leave and company paid enhanced DBS.</strong></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
