   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>We an exciting opportunity available to join a small team in the Brighton area supporting a 1:1 client. We are seeking female only applicants for this role. Please note that you will be required to do 2-3 sleep in shifts each week, and will be paid a flat rate for these on top of your full time hours. </p><p>We are committed to providing personalised support that empowers individuals with complex needs to live independently and with dignity. In this role, you’ll make a real difference by helping people achieve their goals, promoting social inclusion, and managing risks with compassion and professionalism.</p><p>Our team comprises of many different types of extra-ordinary people; we are not looking for one ‘set’ of skills but instead are looking for people who share our vision to do something different; something innovative, high quality and something that achieves something amazing for the people we work with.</p><p>Whether you’re new to the field or building on existing experience, you’ll find excellent opportunities to grow your skills and progress your career within a supportive and award-winning organisation.</p><p>This is your chance to be part of a meaningful journey that transforms lives every day!</p><p>We do not offer sponsorship with this role.</p><br><strong>About the Role</strong><p>You will have the full support of a team leader who will be actively involved in the service and benefit from our extensive training and development. You will also have access to our in-house clinical team to provide any additional advice and guidance you may need, as well as client/diagnosis specific training.</p><p>We are looking for staff with experience in mental health, or transferrable skills within a similar field. You must be able to work autonomously from the detailed support plans provided for each client to work flexibly across the many services we provide for clients with all levels of need within the mental health spectrum. You need to be resilient, adaptable, as well as confident in problem solving a variety of situations and presentations.</p><p>We provide support in a recovery focused way, always aiming to practice Trauma Informed support. Our goal is to guide our clients to regain or rebuild their independence and control over their own lives, helping them increase their confidence in themselves to be able to make their own decisions.</p><p>Key Duties:</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
