   "description": "<p>Gain real NHS experience, learn from dedicated professionals and begin building your long-term healthcare career - it all starts here.</p><p>Looking for a role where you can make a difference and build a future in healthcare? Start your NHS Career as a Healthcare Support Worker!</p><p>We are looking for mental health support workers in both Southsea and Gosport.</p><p>The Orchards at St James hospital in Southsea have 2 wards Hawthorn is for Acute Admissions and the Maples is for Psychiatric Intensive Care. They both primarily look after working age adults (18-65 years) experiencing acute episodes of mental health crisis and placed on a Section of the mental health act.</p><p>We have positions available within our Older Persons Mental Health (OPMH)teams based at Gosport War Memorial Hospital(Poppy & Rose) and St James Hospital(Brooker).</p><p>Older Persons Mental Health (OPMH) wards cater primarily for people over the age of 65. The multidisciplinary team provide care for older adults requiring assessment and treatment for an acute phase of a mental health needs, or a mental illness causing severely challenging behaviour that means they are unable to look after themselves or be looked after at home.</p><p>There is space later in the application to tell us your preferred service and location..</p><p>At this time we are unable to offer sponsorship for these roles</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>You'll work closely with patients, their families and carers, playing a vital part in ensuring everyone who uses our services has a positive and supportive experience. As part of a multi-disciplinary team, you'll work alongside nurses, activity coordinators, social workers, occupational therapists and psychiatrists, offering you a unique chance to learn from different specialties every day. Every shift is an opportunity to develop your knowledge.</p><p>*Work as an integral member of a multidisciplinary team, supporting service users to build independence and develop daily living skills, including personal hygiene, diet and fluids and participation in social or leisure activities as outlined in their Care Plan.</p><p>*Provide support in risk management, develop therapeutic relationships and help individuals lead meaningful and fulfilling lives.</p><p>*Act as a role model for colleagues, offering guidance and support to new or less experienced team members.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
