   "description": "<b>Package Description: </b><strong>A career where your kindness could brighten someone's day</strong><p>Join our Beaufort care home team as a Care Assistant and make a real difference in residents’ lives while building a rewarding career in care, no experience necessary.</p><p>All you need is compassion and the right to work in the UK. We’ll provide fully funded training and excellent career development to help you grow.</p><p>And the best part? You’ll get just as much back, the gratitude, the stories, the smiles that stay with you, plus:</p><strong>You’ll receive:</strong><ul><li>Outstanding career development with fully funded training and qualifications (up to QCF Level 5)</li><li>36 hours per week to include alternating weekends</li><li>Days and nights currently available </li><li>Refer-a-Friend scheme – earn up to £1,000*</li><li>Up to £12.76 per hour</li><li>Blue Light Card discounts</li><li>Company pension scheme</li><li>On-demand pay</li></ul><strong>The role of a Care Assistant:</strong><ul><li>Provide high-quality personal care and support to residents.</li><li>Assist with medication administration and recording.</li><li>Support residents with daily living activities and routines.</li><li>Build meaningful relationships and provide companionship.</li><li>Help enrich residents' lives through activities, hobbies, and social engagement.</li><li>Promote residents' dignity, independence, and well-being.</li><li>Work as part of a caring team to deliver outstanding person-centred care</li></ul><strong>About you:<br>You don’t need previous care experience. What matters most is your kindness and motivation to help others.</strong><ul><li>No experience needed – full training provided</li><li>Compassionate, patient and great with people</li><li>Minimum 12 months right to work in the UK (we cannot currently offer sponsorship)</li><li>Able to work alternate weekends</li></ul><p>Whether you’re listening to residents’ wonderful life stories, helping with daily routines, or simply being a friendly face that brightens their day, you’ll be making a real difference to their lives.</p><strong>Where you'll be working:</strong><p>Beaufort Park Retirement Village,7 Rectory Rd, Burnham-on-Sea TA8 2BY</p><p>Care home: </p><p>Apply to be a Care Assistant, where compassion meets purpose.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
