   "description": "<p><strong>Healthcare Support Worker (HSCW)</strong></p> <p><strong>Hospital of St Cross &amp; University Hospital Coventry</strong></p> <p>Supporting the Registered Nursing staff in the delivery of personal care and assistance for patients at The Hospital of St Cross &amp; University Hospital Coventry.</p> <p>Please beadvised, interviewswill be held on the13th November 2026,at University Hospital Coventry &amp; Warwickshire, Clinical Science Building for shortlisted candidates.</p> <p>Please note this vacancy is for substantive staff only, we are not currently recruiting for bankpositions.</p> <p><strong><em>The post holder will be required to work flexibly to meet the needs of the service. This may include working across a range of shift patterns, including evenings, weekends, and bank holidays where appropriate.</em></strong></p> <p><strong><em>Candidates who have previously applied for this post within the last 3 months and were not successful need not apply.</em></strong></p> <p><strong><em>Successful applicants willbe requiredto provide an immunisation and vaccination report, from either their current UK occupational health provider or their UK GP.</em></strong></p> <p><strong><em>Sponsorship is unable to be supported with this role.</em></strong></p> <p><strong><em>Closing Date: Please be advised that this job advert will close as soon as sufficient applications have been received. Please apply for this job as soon as you can, if interested.</em></strong></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>Do you want to become part of a team who make a difference on a daily basis, providing high quality patient centred care?</p> <p>We are looking to recruit passionate and enthusiastic people who either hold a health and social care qualification BTEC level 2 or above or have experience in a person-centred &amp; public facing role to become a healthcare support worker at Hospital of St Cross &amp; University Hospital Coventry.</p> <p>If you have excellent communication skills, have a caring and compassionate nature, have the desire to help others and the drive to develop a rewarding career you will be proud of, then we want to hear from you.</p> <p>If successful you will become a valued colleague at UHCW with your development needs supported by a robust week-long induction, mandatory enrolment on the \"Time to Care programme\" &amp; Care Certificate Qualification.</p> <p>For more Information on the role of a HCSW- please see the attached document</p></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
