   "description": "<p>Are you passionate about supporting people to live fulfilling, meaningful lives? If so, we would love to hear from you.</p> <p>Shieling is a purpose-built home providing specialist support for seven gentlemen with a learning disability and a range of associated needs, including Autistic<strong> </strong>Spectrum Disorder (ASD), mental health needs, sensory impairments, and epilepsy.</p> <p>At Shieling, we pride ourselves on providing a therapeutic, person-centred approach within a warm, welcoming, and homely environment. Our focus is on ensuring the people we support are at the heart of everything we do, empowering them to make choices, achieve personal goals, and lead happy, fulfilling lives. In this role, you'll be part of a supportive team where your contribution truly matters. You'll have the opportunity to build rewarding relationships, develop your skills, and help people achieve outcomes that enrich their lives.</p> <p><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p> <p>We are seeking caring, positive, and motivated individuals who are committed to making a difference. Previous experience within social care is desirable, but most importantly, we are looking for people who share our values and have a genuine passion for supporting others.</p> <p>You will be:</p> <ul> <li>Compassionate and person-centred in your approach.</li> <li>Committed to promoting independence and inclusion.</li> <li>A strong team player with excellent communication skills.</li> <li>Respectful of individual differences and choices.</li> </ul> <p></p> <p></p> <p></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><ul> <li>Support people using our services in line with their individual care plan to promote as much independence as possible.</li> <li>To assist with all aspects of personal care (supporting continence needs, showering, bathing etc.) in accordance with individual's support needs.</li> <li>Participate in the ongoing monitoring of the health (mental and physical) and behaviour of people using the service.</li> <li>Reporting and recording all relevant information and reporting to Shift Leader any changes in the person.</li> <li>Act as a keyworker for named individuals within the service.</li> <li>Support an active and enjoyable lifestyle of individuals, by encouraging a range of leisure and social interests. Support on holidays, as identified in their person-centred plans.</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
