   "expires": "2026-11-01",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>The Community Learning Disabilities Team on the Isle of Wight are seeking applications from highly motivated individuals to work as a Support Worker within the Intensive Support Team. This a permanent, part-time position at 30.75 hours per week.</p><p>The post holder will be able to focus on the direct needs of the service users, working across boundaries of care an organisations; develop a rapport based upon companionship and friendship and be able to assist practitioners within the Intensive Support Team to assess, plan, implement and evaluate individual care plans.</p><p>Please contact Rachel Pragnell for more information. We look forward to receiving your applications!</p><p>At present, the Trust is unable to offer Skilled Worker visa sponsorship for this post. Applicants must have the right to work in the UK at the time of application.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>*To provide support and give time to an allocated group of service users in order to promote their safety and maintain them in the community environment.</p><p>*To support service users to identify their needs and to assist practitioners within the Intensive Support Team to assess, plan, implement and evaluate individual care plans.</p><p>*To have the individual service users' needs at the fore at all times and use agreed values and skills to underpin their day-to-day work.</p><p>*To assist the practitioners in administering agreed standards of care to all service users.</p><p>*To be responsible for building a rapport with service users which may entail working with them in a setting other than that of the service user's home i.e.: visiting community resources.</p><p>*Answer the telephone and take messages, maintaining confidentiality and referring relevant calls to qualified staff.</p><p>*To help identify early signs of relapse by monitoring the service user's progress, level of functioning and mental state and alert the appropriate staff involved in the service users care.</p><p>*Actively participate as necessary in risk assessment and risk management practises, in line with Risk Policy.</p><p>*Attend outpatient appointments and clinical reviews with selected service users as required.</p><p>*Encourage and assist service users in leisure, social and recreational activities.</p><p>*To support service users to engage effectively with the agreed care plan and access appropriate services provided on a regular basis.</p></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
