   "expires": "2026-11-05",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>We are seeking a motivated and compassionate Physical Health Care Assistant to join our Community Mental Health Team. This is an exciting opportunity to support the delivery of high-quality physical healthcare for adults receiving secondary mental health services.</p> <p>You will work alongside nurses, doctors, allied health professionals and support staff to improve the physical health and wellbeing of service users with serious mental illness. The role will involve carrying out physical health assessments, monitoring physical health indicators and supporting individuals to access appropriate healthcare services.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p>Main Duties and Responsibilities <ul> <li>Undertake physical health monitoring including blood pressure, pulse, weight, BMI and other routine observations.</li> <li>Support the completion of annual physical health checks for service users.</li> <li>Perform venepuncture and ECGs (or undertake training where required).</li> <li>Record and maintain accurate clinical records in line with Trust policies.</li> <li>Support service users to engage with physical health initiatives and healthy lifestyle interventions.</li> <li>Liaise with GPs, primary care services and other healthcare professionals as appropriate.</li> <li>Escalate concerns regarding a service user's physical or mental health to the appropriate clinician.</li> <li>Participate in team meetings, supervision and mandatory training.</li> </ul></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>Welcome to Birmingham and Solihull Mental Health NHS Foundation Trust. Our 4000 clinical and support staff help us to improve mental health wellbeing and meet the needs of the 70,000 people we serve each year. We provide a range of mental healthcare services across Birmingham and Solihull, as well as specialised services nationally. We also offer medical, nursing and psychology training and are proud of our international reputation for both research and innovation.</p>\n<p>Our population is culturally diverse, characterised in places by high levels of deprivation which create an increasing demand for our services and a necessity for us to make sure everyone can access the help they need. We are a team of compassionate, inclusive and committed people working together to provide excellent care to support our community. If you are looking for a place to belong, where you can make a real difference to people's lives, join our team where our warm welcome is waiting for you.</p></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
