   "salaryText": "£13.71 per hour",
   "posted": "2026-10-20",
   "expires": "2026-12-01",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>We are looking for warm, caring people to join Westmeads, our extra care service in Royston, Barnsley. You’ll provide personalised care and support that helps older residents stay independent, active and connected to their community.</p> <p>In this rewarding role, you’ll offer dignified personal care, emotional support and help with daily living, including meals, hydration, household tasks and safe medication support. You’ll encourage residents to take part in activities, maintain relationships and enjoy a fulfilling, independent lifestyle. You’ll respond to changing needs, support wellbeing and work positively with families, health professionals and housing partners to ensure each person receives coordinated, person-centred care.</p> <p><strong>Looking for a new Career in Care? We Provide the Training!</strong></p> <p><strong>No Previous Experience Needed</strong></p> <p>We provide all of your training as you begin your new career in care, including the opportunity to work towards earning your QCF Diploma in Health and Social Care. All employees have access to our training system where, through a combination of in person and e-learning courses, you can learn the skills required to develop in your role and progress toward senior roles.</p> <p>We are looking for individuals with compassion, reliability and a strong sense of responsibility. You’ll need good communication skills, the ability to record information clearly, and the physical capability to support people with moving and positioning. Shifts include mornings, afternoons, evenings and waking nights, and flexibility is expected to meet the needs of the service.</p> <p>Full-time roles are 37.5 hours per week; part-time roles start from 15 hours. All hours are worked flexibly on a rota including evenings, weekends and public holidays.</p> <p><strong>Vacancy Reference Number:</strong><strong>90717</strong></p> <p>Applications for this role must be submitted via the Creative Support website using the above vacancy reference number</p> <p><strong>Benefits of working with Creative Support include a probationary bonus, pension contributions, 28 days Annual Leave and company paid enhanced DBS.</strong></p> <p>We are a passionate, inclusive, and anti-racist organization – Stonewall Diversity Champion, Disability Confident Employer who have recently received Investors in People Gold award.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
