   "description": "<p>We are seeking warm, reliable and proactive full and part time Support Workers for our learning disabilities supported living services in Stockport. We provide person-centred care to enable people with a learning disability to enjoy active and fulfilled lives.</p> <p>You will support service users by providing respectful personal care and support with daily living tasks at home and varied activities in the community. Some of the people we support have health or behaviour support needs and will need your skilled support to maintain their health and wellbeing.</p> <p>You will be expected to use personalised communication approaches and to develop trusting relationships with the people we support and their families.</p> <p>In most of our services you will undertake sleep-ins. You must be willing to cover various shift patterns (early and late shifts), depending on the needs of the people we support, across a 7-day rota. In most of our services you will also undertake sleep-ins for which we pay an additional sleep-in allowance.</p> <p><strong>Looking for a new Career in Care? We Provide the Training!</strong></p> <p><strong>No Previous Experience Needed!</strong></p> <p>We provide all of your training as you begin your new career in care, including the opportunity to work towards earning your QCF Diploma in Health and Social Care. All employees have access to our training system where, through a combination of in person and e-learning courses, you can learn the skills required to develop in your role and progress toward senior roles.</p> <p><strong>Possession of a full UK driving licence is essential for this role.</strong></p> <p><strong>Vacancy Reference Number: 97032</strong></p> <p>Applications for this role must be submitted via the Creative Support website using the above vacancy reference number.</p> <p>Benefits of working with Creative Support include a probationary bonus, pension contributions, 28 days Annual Leave and company paid enhanced DBS.</p> <p>We are a passionate, inclusive, and anti-racist organization – Stonewall Diversity Champion, Disability Confident Employer who have recently received an Investors in People Gold award.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
