   "expires": "2026-11-01",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>The Patient Flow Support Worker is an integral member of the Patient Flow team, providing practical and administrative support to help facilitate the safe, effective and timely movement of patients through the hospital.</p> <p>The post holder will work closely with Patient Flow colleagues, ward teams, clinical services, discharge teams and relevant partner organisations to support the coordination of patient pathways and discharge activity. They will assist with maintaining accurate and up-to-date patient information, following up agreed actions, identifying potential delays and escalating issues appropriately.</p> <p>The role requires excellent communication and organisational skills, with the ability to work effectively in a busy and changing operational environment. The post holder will manage competing priorities, maintain confidentiality and provide a professional and responsive service to colleagues, patients and external partners.</p> <p>Through effective coordination and administrative support, the Patient Flow Support Worker will contribute to <strong>reducing avoidable delays, supporting timely discharge, improving patient flow and helping the organisation make the best use of available bed capacity.</strong></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>The Patient Flow Support Worker will provide day-to-day operational and administrative support to the Patient Flow team, helping to ensure patients move safely and efficiently through the hospital.</p> <p>Key duties include supporting the coordination of patient discharges, transfers and repatriations; liaising with ward teams, clinical staff, therapists, discharge services and external partners to progress patient pathways; and identifying and escalating delays or barriers to discharge.</p> <p>The post holder will use <strong>OPTICA and WardBoard</strong> daily to monitor patient pathways, maintain accurate discharge information and undertake reconciliation between systems, following up discrepancies and outstanding actions.</p> <p>The role will also support patient transport arrangements, operational and discharge meetings, data collection and general administrative duties. The post holder will respond to telephone and email enquiries, maintain accurate and confidential patient records, and work flexibly in response to changing operational pressures.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
