   "salaryText": "£25,760 to £27,476 a year pro-rata",
   "band": "Band 3",
   "posted": "2026-10-19",
   "expires": "2026-11-02",
   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>We are looking for a caring, motivated Healthcare Support Worker to join our friendly multidisciplinary team, providing care to patients in their own homes and residential care settings.</p> <p>The Role</p> <p>You will:</p> <p> Carry out independent visits to patients in the community.</p> <p> Deliver high-quality, person-centred care.</p> <p> Work closely with nurses, therapists and other members of the multidisciplinary team.</p> <p> Monitor and report changes in patients' conditions.</p> <p></p> <p> What we are looking for:</p> <p> A wide range of healthcare support skills.</p> <p> Ability to work independently and as part of a team.</p> <p> Good communication and organisational skills.</p> <p> Ombersley and Rural patch.</p> <p></p> <p> Working Hours</p> <p>This is a 7-day service with shifts starting at 7:30 am, 9:00 am or 10:30 am. The latest finish time is 6:30 pm, including weekend and bank holiday working on a rota basis.</p> <p>If you enjoy community working and making a difference to patients' lives, we'd love to hear from you.</p> <p>Applicants must read the attached guidance notes before submitting your application for full understanding of Trust requirements.</p> <p></p> <p></p> <p></p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>As a Band 3 Healthcare Support Worker within the team, you will provide high-quality, person-centred care to patients in their own homes, supporting them to maintain their independence and wellbeing. Working under the direction of registered nurses, you will assist with personal care, monitoring and recording observations, wound care, catheter care, simple dressings, and other delegated clinical tasks. You will identify and report changes in patients' conditions, maintain accurate clinical records, and contribute to care planning. The role involves travelling between patients' homes, working collaboratively with the wider multidisciplinary team, and promoting dignity, respect and patient choice always. You will also support health promotion, infection prevention and ensure equipment is used safely in line with Trust policies.</p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>At Herefordshire and Worcestershire Health and Care NHS Trust, we are working together to deliver outstanding care. We run community hospitals and community health services across Worcestershire and provide mental health and learning disability services across both Herefordshire and Worcestershire.</p> <p></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
