   "description": "<p><strong>Family Support Worker Part Time </strong></p> <p><strong>Coventry</strong><br><strong>£12,602 per annum</strong><br><strong>18.5 Hours per Week</strong><br><strong>Permanent</strong></p> <p><strong>Make a Difference to Families in Your Community</strong></p> <p>We are looking for a compassionate and dedicated <strong>Family Support Worker</strong> to join a specialist service supporting women, children and families affected by domestic abuse.</p> <p>This rewarding role involves providing practical and emotional support to families, helping them improve their safety, wellbeing and independence. You will work closely with service users to identify needs, develop support plans and access the services required to achieve positive outcomes.</p> <p><strong>The Role</strong></p> <p>As a Family Support Worker, you will manage a caseload of families and provide person-centred support tailored to individual circumstances. You will work collaboratively with statutory and voluntary agencies to ensure children and families receive the right support at the right time.</p> <p><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p> <ul> <li>Provide one-to-one support to women, children and families.</li><li>Complete needs assessments, risk assessments and support plans.</li><li>Support families affected by domestic abuse and other complex challenges.</li><li>Safeguard children and vulnerable adults.</li><li>Advocate on behalf of service users with partner agencies.</li><li>Support access to housing, education, healthcare and community services.</li><li>Work closely with Social Care, schools and external professionals.</li><li>Maintain accurate and confidential case records.</li><li>Contribute to positive outcomes for families and children.</li></ul> <p><strong>Requirements</strong></p> <ul> <li>Experience supporting vulnerable families, children or individuals.</li><li>Experience within family support, domestic abuse, social care or community services.</li><li>Knowledge of safeguarding and child protection.</li><li>Strong communication and advocacy skills.</li><li>Experience managing a caseload and support planning.</li><li>Ability to work independently and as part of a team.</li><li>Good IT and record-keeping skills.</li><li>Understanding of equality, diversity and inclusion.</li></ul> <p><strong>Desirable</strong></p> <ul> <li>Relevant Health & Social Care qualification.</li><li>Experience supporting BAMER communities.</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
