   "description": "<p><strong>Healthcare Support Worker Band 2 to 3 development role.</strong></p><p><strong>Salary: £25,272 pro rata per annum.</strong></p><p><strong>Work Location: St Mary's Hosp (IOW), Parkhurst Road, Newport, Isle of Wight, PO30 5TG, Newport, United Kingdom, PO30 5TG.</strong></p><p><strong>Hours per week: Full time, 37.5 hours per week (will consider part time, minimum 23 hours).</strong></p><p><strong>Contract Type: Permanent.</strong></p><p>Whether you're new to care or already have experience, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p>As a Healthcare Support Worker (HCSW), you'll play a vital role in helping patients feel safe, supported and cared for during their stay in hospital. If you're compassionate, reliable, enjoy working with people and want a career that truly matters, this could be the perfect opportunity.</p><p>No previous healthcare experience is essential. We'll provide full training, support and development to help you succeed in your role.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><p>Why join us?</p><ul><li>Full support through a comprehensive two week induction programme</li> <li>Opportunity to complete the Care Certificate</li> <li>Learn valuable healthcare skills and gain NHS experience</li> <li>Work as part of a friendly and supportive team</li> <li>Excellent opportunities for career development within the NHS</li> <li>Have a career for life</li> <li>Shift enhancements for evenings, nights and weekends</li></ul><p>Working alongside registered healthcare professionals, you'll support patients with their day to day care and wellbeing, helping them maintain their dignity, comfort and independence.</p></p> <h4>About us</h4> <p><p>Working for our Trust brings a variety of benefits, including an onsite day nursery, cycle-to-work scheme, discounts at local businesses and gyms, and the opportunity to hire Trusts beach hut in Ryde. We offer many flexible working opportunities, speak to us about how we might be able to accommodate a flexible working arrangement for you and if it works for the service, we will do our best to make it work for you.</p><p><strong>Please upload a copy of Maths and English (GCSE or equivalent International) qualifications to your application, without this information you will not be invited to interview.</strong></p></p> <h4>Details</h4> <h4>Date posted</h4> <p>16 October 2026</p> <h4>Pay scheme</h4> <p>Agenda for change</p> <h4>Band</h4> <p>Band 2</p> <h4>Salary</h4> <p> £25,272 a year </p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
