   "description": "<p><strong>Support Worker Waking Nights | West Malling </strong></p> <p><strong>Part time 30 hours per week 10pm – 7am | Any driving license is required </strong></p> <p><strong>Make a Difference While the World Sleeps</strong></p> <p>At Avenues, people smile, laugh, grow and achieve together. We believe that when our teams feel valued, supported and empowered, they help the people we support live happy, fulfilling and independent lives.</p> <p>We're looking for a compassionate and reliable Waking Night Support Worker to join our team in West Malling, supporting seven adults with learning disabilities, autism and behaviours of concern.</p> <p>Working waking nights is about much more than being present. You'll play a vital role in providing reassurance, promoting wellbeing and ensuring the people we support remain safe, comfortable and supported throughout the night. Every shift helps give the people we support – and their families – peace of mind.</p> <p><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></p> <p>During your waking night shifts, you'll:</p> <ul> <li>Provide overnight support, ensuring the safety and wellbeing of the people we support</li><li>Carry out regular wellbeing checks and respond to any support needs during the night</li><li>Deliver respectful, person-centred personal care where required</li><li>Support with evening and morning routines, helping people prepare for bed and start their day</li><li>Complete accurate records and handovers to the daytime team</li><li>Help maintain a safe, clean and welcoming home environment</li><li>Promote dignity, independence and choice at all times</li></ul> <p>No two nights are ever the same, and you'll be an important part of helping people feel safe and supported around the clock.</p> <p><strong>Why Join Avenues?</strong></p> <p>We invest in our people and offer a fantastic range of benefits, including:</p> <ul> <li>Early Pay – access part of your earned wages before payday</li><li>Fully paid Enhanced DBS</li><li>Flexible working patterns</li><li>Paid annual leave (pro rata)</li><li>Award-winning training and ongoing development opportunities</li><li>Clear career progression pathways</li><li>Contributory pension scheme with life assurance</li><li>Blue Light Card and Benefits website discounts on shopping, travel, entertainment and more</li><li>Recommend a Friend scheme – earn up to <strong>£500</strong></li><li>24/7 health and wellbeing support, including confidential counselling services</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
