   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p>We are looking for an enthusiastic, dynamic, motivated and flexible Healthcare Support Worker to join our integrated sexual health service. We provide screening and treatment of sexually transmitted infections, HIV care and contraception to a diverse population of clients.</p><p>This vacancy is for 37.5 hours - The main base will be U6, Eastleigh, but there will be a requirement to cover other clinics in the North locality as and when required(Andover and Basingstoke).</p><p>In return you will become a valued member of a team known for its innovation and high standard of care. You will be supported to complete in house training by a line manager and HCSW 'mentor'. You will have regular one to one meetings and appraisals to monitor your progress and development needs. In addition, the service offers regular education sessions and clinical supervision.</p><p>For this post, you will need to be able to travel between sites.</p><p>The successful candidate may have some previous experience working as a Healthcare Support Worker or in a sexual health environment but this is not essential. People skills and a willingness to learn are paramount.</p><p>You will be expected to work in sexual health clinics across North Hampshire and on occasion, and dependent on the needs of the service, we may ask you to support other clinics across our Hampshire sites. You may be required to support a clinic in HMP Winchester on occasion.</p></p> <h4>Main duties of the job</h4> <p><ul><li>Collect and process a variety of specimens.</li><li>Perform venepuncture</li><li>Undertake basic observations of patients, including blood pressure.</li><li>Manage asymptomatic patients.</li><li>Able to assist the Clinician during IUD fittings</li><li>Processes routine samples by labelling, recording, and storing appropriately</li><li>Performs light microscopy for sexually transmitted infections</li><li>Maintains stock levels and orders stock as necessary</li><li>Travels to spoke clinics or other locations within Sexual Health</li><li>Administrative duties as required, including reception tasks</li><li>Develop rapport with patients and treat all patients, carers and staff with dignity and respect</li><li>Frequently use interpersonal and communication skills to de-escalate and reduce aggressive behaviour if encountered from patients and carers</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
