   "description": "<strong>Clinical Support Worker</strong><strong>Band 3</strong><p>Main area<br><br>Clinical Support Worker</p><p>Grade<br><br>Band 3</p><p>Contract<br><br>Permanent</p><p>Hours</p><ul><li>Full time</li><li>Part time</li></ul><p>37.5 hours per week (Shifts may include Days, Nights or Twilights)</p><p>Job ref<br><br>373-SMH2790</p><p>Site<br><br>Springview Hospital</p><p>Town<br><br>Wirral</p><p>Salary<br><br>£25,760 - £27,476 per annum</p><p>Salary period<br><br>Yearly</p><p>Closing<br><br>19/10/2026 23:59</p><strong>Job overview</strong><p><strong>If you relish a challenge, are caring and compassionate and have a passion to help others or simply fancy a fresh start, then we need people who share our values and vision to join our team as Clinical Support Workers.</strong></p><p>We are looking for enthusiastic and motivated Band 3 Clinical Support Workers to join our dynamic team on Oaktrees Ward in Springview Hospital in Clatterbridge. We are a 14 bedded Specialist Eating Disorder Unit (SEDU).</p><p>In this role, you'll provide high quality, compassionate care to adults with mental health conditions. You'll work closely with a multi disciplinary team to deliver personalised treatment plans and provide support to patients as they navigate complex mental health challenges.</p><p>We are looking for applicants who have some experience of working with people with mental health diagnoses and who can demonstrate their compassion and optimism for the rehabilitation and recovery of this client group.</p><p>The ward offers a 7 day per week / 24hours per day service, therefore the successful candidates must be able to work a full range of 12 hour shifts including day, night and weekends shifts. The role may also include Twilight or bridging shifts in the evening.</p><p>This is a rewarding and fulfilling position, perfect for a dedicated individual looking to advance their career while making a significant difference.</p><p>We would welcome informal discussions about the role should you wish to contact us.</p><strong>Main duties of the job</strong><p>The postholder works under the direct supervision of a registered nurse and will be expected to assist on all aspects and duties expected in a clinical ward environment.</p><p>Key Responsibilities include:</p><p>Assisting in standardised procedures relating to individualised patient care</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
