   "description": "<p><strong>Support Worker – Clouds House </strong></p><p><strong>Location: </strong>Clouds House</p><p><strong>Salary:</strong> £28,479 per annum</p><p><strong>About The Role</strong></p><p>Looking for work where you can truly make a difference?</p><p>Join the team at Clouds House as a Support Worker, based at Clouds House. You’ll play a vital role in helping people build lasting recovery in a safe, structured and therapeutic residential environment.</p><p>Working within our fully integrated One Team model, you’ll help reinforce our 12-Step and trauma-informed treatment approach. No two shifts are the same – this is a hands-on, rewarding role where your presence, professionalism and compassion matter every day.</p><p><strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong></p><ul><li>Supporting clients to engage in daily routines, wellbeing activities and the therapeutic programme</li><li>Promoting structure, communal responsibilities and positive recovery habits</li><li>Maintaining a safe, respectful and supportive living environment</li><li>Monitoring welfare, safeguarding and behavioural concerns, escalating where needed</li><li>Supporting medication processes (including eMAR where trained)</li><li>Completing accurate, up-to-date records and handovers</li><li>Responding calmly and professionally to incidents or client needs</li><li>Working closely with colleagues across all departments as part of one team</li></ul><p><strong>What we’re looking for:</strong></p><ul><li>Experience in health, social care, recovery or residential settings</li><li>Strong communication and people skills</li><li>Emotional resilience with the ability to remain calm under pressure</li><li>A professional, boundaried and compassionate approach</li><li>Good organisation and attention to detail</li><li>Understanding of safeguarding principles</li><li>Commitment to recovery-focused and trauma-informed practice</li></ul><p><strong>Desirable:</strong></p><ul><li>Experience in addiction or mental health services</li><li>Knowledge of 12-Step recovery models</li><li>Experience managing challenging behaviour</li><li>Full UK Driving Licence</li></ul><p>At Clouds House, you’ll be part of a supportive and passionate team making a genuine difference every day. We offer ongoing training and development opportunities, and the chance to build valuable experience in a rewarding recovery-focused environment where your contribution truly matters.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
