   "description": "<p><br></p><p><strong>Support Worker</strong></p><p><strong>Sutton In Ashfield</strong></p><p><strong>£24,871 - £25,371 per annum</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Are you a caring, friendly individual who wants to get into the world of social care with a reputable, values-based organisation? Would you like to make a real difference in the community as a Support Worker, helping people with learning disabilities live happy, fulfilling and independent lives? Join us!</p><p><br></p><p>Some of your benefits include: </p><p><br></p><ul><li>Salary of £24,871 - £25,371 per annum</li><li>36.5 days annual leave including bank holidays, with the option to buy and sell leave.</li><li>Additional payments for sleep-in shifts</li><li>Comprehensive training and ongoing development opportunities</li><li>A welcoming, inclusive and diverse workplace culture</li><li>Ongoing support from experienced and dedicated colleagues</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Please note that we are not currently offering visa sponsorships.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>The Service</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ashland Road West</strong> is a registered <strong>care home for adults with learning disabilities</strong> located in <strong>Sutton-in-Ashfield, Nottinghamshire</strong>. We provide person-centred care and support to ten service users with moderate to profound learning disabilities, physical disabilities, communication needs and complex healthcare-related requirements. We support people with behaviours that challenge and provide full training to our colleagues to be confident in their support abilities.</p><p><br></p><p>Every day, we do all we can to help our service users be as independent as possible by working together as a team and having their best interests at the heart of everything we do. We are looking for an enthusiastic team player to come and join our family of expert colleagues.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>The Role</strong></p><p><br></p><p>As a <strong>Learning Disability Support Worker</strong>, your role will involve helping service users to live as independently as possible. The life of a <strong>Support Worker</strong> includes supporting service users with personal care, day trips out, playing games, sensory experiences and even watching the odd movie!</p><p><br></p><p>In addition to this, some of your main duties will include but are not limited to:</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Supporting with visits to health appointments, day trips and holidays</li><li>Administering medication</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
