   "description": "<p><strong>Job Title:</strong> Children's Residential Support Worker<br><strong>Location:</strong> 107 Alexandra Road, Wellingborough, Northamptonshire, NN8 1EG, United Kingdom<br><strong>Salary:</strong> £14.50 per hour<br><strong>Job Type:</strong> Full-Time / Part-Time / Permanent (Flexible shifts available)<br><strong>Sector:</strong> Residential Childcare<br><strong>Children's Residential Support Worker</strong><br>Are you passionate about making a positive difference in the lives of children and young people?<br>We are currently recruiting experienced <strong>Children's Residential Support Workers</strong> to join a dedicated and supportive team providing high-quality care for children and young people aged <strong>8-16 years</strong> within a residential setting in <strong>Wellingborough, Northamptonshire</strong>.<br>This is a rewarding opportunity for individuals who are committed to safeguarding, supporting and empowering young people to achieve positive outcomes while providing a safe, nurturing and therapeutic home environment.<br><strong>The Role</strong><br>As a Children's Residential Support Worker, you will play a key role in supporting children and young people with their emotional, behavioural and social development. Working alongside a dedicated team, you will help create a stable, caring and structured environment where every child feels safe, valued and supported.<br>You will build positive relationships with young people while promoting independence, resilience and confidence, helping them develop the skills they need to thrive.<br><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p> <ul> <li>Provide high-quality care and emotional support to children and young people aged 8-16.</li><li>Promote a safe, caring and nurturing home environment.</li><li>Build positive, trusting relationships with young people.</li><li>Support children with their daily routines, personal development and life skills.</li><li>Encourage participation in education, hobbies and community activities.</li><li>Promote positive behaviour using therapeutic and child-centred approaches.</li><li>Assist with care planning and individual support plans.</li><li>Maintain accurate daily records, reports and incident documentation.</li><li>Administer medication where trained and authorised.</li><li>Safeguard children and report any concerns in line with safeguarding procedures.</li><li>Support children during appointments, education and recreational activities.</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
