   "description": "<p><strong>Up to £42,775+ earning potential | 4 on 4 off shift pattern | Career Progression and funded qualifications | North East Based </strong></p><p>At Nova Care Group, we know that supporting a young person through crisis and complexity takes more than experience on paper.</p><p>We know this because our organisation was founded on lived experience. We've seen first hand how much difference the right people, at the right time, can make in a young person's life.</p><p>Now we're looking for people who want to make that difference too.</p><p><strong>The role </strong></p><p>This isn't always an easy job but it will always make a difference. </p><p>The young people we support have experienced significant challenges in their lives and often communicate their experiences through behaviours such as aggression, absconding, sexualised behaviours, self-harm, criminalisation or withdrawing from others. </p><p>Your role is to stay calm, consistent and compassionate. To set clear boundaries, build trust and look beyond the behaviour to understand what a young person may be experiencing. </p><p>There will be challenging times, difficult conversations and times when progress feels slow. Then there are the moments that make it all worthwhile.</p><p>Seeing a young person begin to trust you, watching them manage something they couldn't before, seeing their confidence grow, their behaviour stabilise or taking another step towards independence.</p><p><strong>Requirements for our Support Workers:</strong></p><p>If you've worked in a demanding environment where you've had to remain calm under pressure, you'll already have many of the skills we're looking for. You’ll be: </p><ul><li>Fully flexible and able to work and travel across the North East</li><li>Able to work 12 hours shifts, covering days, waking nights and sleep in shifts. </li><li>In possession of a Full UK Driving licence and right to work in the UK (we are not able to offer sponsorship)</li></ul><p><strong>What you'll receive:</strong></p><ul><li>£30,000–£32,000 basic salary</li><li>Shift enhancements with earning potential of £42,775+</li><li>A 4 on 4 off shift pattern, giving you regular blocks of time away from work</li><li>Enhanced annual leave, increasing with length of service</li><li>Private healthcare cover</li><li>Team bonus opportunities</li><li>Fully funded Level 3 and Level 4 NVQ qualifications</li><li>Clear career and progression pathways</li><li>Paid sick leave</li><li>Company pension scheme</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
