   "description": "<p><strong>Personal Care Assistant (SEND) - Term Time Only</strong><br><strong>Hayes, West London</strong><br><strong>£24,572 Actual Salary</strong><br><strong>36 Hours per Week | 39 Weeks per Year (Term Time Only)</strong><br><strong>Monday to Friday, 8:45am - 4:30pm (4:15pm Friday)</strong></p> <p><br>BS Social Care is delighted to be recruiting on behalf of a well-established education provider for a <strong>Personal Care Assistant</strong> to join a brand-new specialist SEND provision in Hayes.<br>This is an exciting opportunity to make a genuine difference in the lives of young adults with complex learning disabilities and additional needs, supporting them to achieve greater independence, wellbeing, and educational success within a highly inclusive learning environment.</p> <p><br><strong>The Role</strong><br>As a Personal Care Assistant, you will work as part of a dedicated Learning Support Team, providing high-quality personal care and daily living support to students with a range of complex physical, medical, and learning needs.<br>You will play a vital role in ensuring students can access learning safely and comfortably while promoting dignity, independence, and choice.</p> <p><br><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p> <ul> <li>Providing personal care support including hygiene, toileting, continence care, dressing, and grooming</li><li>Supporting with eating, drinking, feeding, and nutritional requirements</li><li>Administering and prompting medication in line with care plans</li><li>Using hoists and manual handling equipment safely and appropriately</li><li>Supporting students who use wheelchairs, walkers, and other mobility aids</li><li>Assisting with physiotherapy programmes following training and guidance</li><li>Monitoring and reporting changes in wellbeing, behaviour, or physical condition</li><li>Contributing to and reviewing care plans and risk assessments</li><li>Keeping accurate records of care delivery and medication administration</li><li>Providing emotional support and building positive professional relationships with students</li><li>Working collaboratively with families, therapists, healthcare professionals, and education staff</li><li>Supporting safeguarding and promoting the welfare of vulnerable young people</li></ul> <p><strong>About You</strong><br>To be considered, you must have experience supporting individuals with learning disabilities, SEND, or complex care needs.</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
