   "skills": [],
   "description": "<p><strong>Make a Real Difference Every Day</strong></p><p><strong>Mental Health Support Worker</strong></p><p> <strong>Transitional Support, Oxford</strong><br><br> <strong>£28,938 - £32,214 per annum</strong> (depending on experience)<br><br> <strong>37 hours per week</strong> | Monday – Friday, inclusive of bank holidays, Occasional Evening & Weekends, with occasional covering of shifts. You will be required to participate in an on-call rota as part of this role.</p><p>At Response, we believe everyone deserves the opportunity to live a happy, healthy and fulfilling life.</p><p>We're looking for compassionate, motivated people who want to support others, champion independence, and build a rewarding career in mental health.</p><p>Whether you're starting out in care, considering a career change, or already have experience supporting people, we'll give you the training, skills and support you need to make a genuine difference.</p><p><strong>Why This Role Matters</strong></p><p>As a <strong>Mental Health Support Worker</strong>, you'll help people living with serious mental health challenges build confidence, develop life skills, and move towards greater independence.</p><p>No two days are the same. One day you could be supporting someone to attend an appointment, learn budgeting skills, or take part in activities they enjoy. Another day you could be helping someone achieve an important personal goal they've been working towards.</p><p>The relationships you build and the support you provide can have a lasting impact on someone's recovery journey.</p><p><strong>What You'll Be Doing</strong></p><p>You'll:</p><p> Support residents with daily living skills, wellbeing and independence</p><p> Build positive, trusting relationships</p><p> Encourage people to achieve personal goals, access education, employment and community opportunities</p><p> Work alongside healthcare professionals, families and support networks</p><p> Promote mental and physical wellbeing</p><p> Help create a safe, welcoming and inclusive environment</p><p> Learn and apply therapeutic approaches including Talk Therapy, Motivational Interviewing and Trauma-Informed Care</p><p><strong>What's In It For You?</strong></p><p>We're invested in your career and wellbeing.</p><p> 37 days annual leave (including bank holidays)</p><p> Fully funded training and professional development</p><p> Professional qualification sponsorship</p><p> Blue Light Card discounts</p><p> Free counselling and wellbeing support</p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
