   "description": "<p>We have two exciting opportunities for our accommodation service in Littlehampton. We are seeking 1 part time day Mental Health Support Worker, and 1 full time Waking Nights Mental Health Support Worker. If you think you would be a good fit and you are interested in either of these roles, please get in touch for more detail.</p><p>We are seeking a compassionate and reliable full time Waking Night Mental Health Support Worker to provide overnight support to individuals with mental health needs, ensuring their safety, wellbeing, and comfort throughout the night.</p><p>We are also seeking a compassionate and reliable part time day staff Mental Health Support Worker to work alongside our team to support individuals with mental health needs, promoting independence and support. </p><p>This is a rewarding role where you will make a real difference by offering reassurance, practical assistance, and emotional support during challenging times.</p><p>Our team comprises many different types of extra-ordinary people; we are not looking for one ‘set’ of skills but instead are looking for people who share our vision to do something different; something innovative, high quality and something that achieves something amazing for the people we work with.</p><br><strong>About the Role</strong><p><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li>Provide person-centred care and emotional support during waking night shifts.</li><li>Monitor wellbeing and respond to any incidents calmly and professionally.</li><li>Assist with night-time routines and personal care where required.</li><li>Maintain accurate records and communicate effectively with day staff for continuity of care.</li><li>Promote independence and recovery-focused approaches.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul><li>Enthusiasm for working in mental health and supporting vulnerable individuals.</li><li>Excellent communication skills and a calm, patient approach.</li><li>Ability to work independently and as part of a team.</li><li>Previous experience in mental health or social care is desirable</li><li>Right to work in the UK (we cannot offer sponsorship for this role).</li></ul><br><strong>Benefits</strong><ul><li>You will receive full induction training and continued professional development</li><li>Excellent support from experienced management and the wider clinical leadership team</li></ul><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
