   "description": "<p><b>Social Care Assistant </b></p><p><em><b>Location</b></em>: Hull, East Yorkshire, HU9 1DN<br><em><b>Salary</b></em>: £12.96 per hour + £50 per sleep-in shift<br><em><b>Contract</b></em>: Permanent – Full-time available<br><em><b>Shifts</b></em>: 24/7 rota – 12–14-hour shifts, including early, late and night shifts</p><p><em><b>Please Note – We as a company cannot facilitate any candidates needing sponsorship. </b></em></p><p><b>The Opportunity</b></p><p>Avocet Trust is looking for caring and committed Social Care Assistants / Support Workers to join our team supporting adults with learning disabilities and complex needs.</p><p>No previous experience in social care is required. We provide full training, induction and ongoing support, making this a great opportunity for anyone looking to build a rewarding career in care.</p><p>Full-time roles involve a 24/7 rota with shifts that can vary between 12 and 14 hours, including early, late and night shifts. Part-time opportunities are also available.</p><p><b>Who We Are</b></p><p>Established in 1991, Avocet Trust is a leading charity providing Residential, Short Stay and Day Care services for vulnerable adults.</p><p>With over 40 properties across Hull and the East Riding, we're committed to delivering compassionate, person-centred support and helping the people we support live fulfilling and independent lives.</p><p><b>What You'll Do</b></p><p>• Provide compassionate, person-centred care and support.<br>• Support individuals with daily living, including personal care, meals and household tasks.<br>• Act as a Key Worker and help maintain individual care plans.<br>• Support with medication administration and supervision.<br>• Encourage social activities and community involvement.<br>• Support individuals on holidays, trips and other activities.<br>• Build positive relationships with the people we support.<br>• Communicate effectively with families, healthcare professionals and colleagues.</p><p><b>What We're Looking For</b></p><p>No previous care experience That's okay! We welcome applications from people from a wide range of backgrounds who have transferable skills and a genuine desire to help others.</p><p><b>You'll need:</b></p><p><i>Shortened here. The full description is on the original advert.</i></p>",
